    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Les-Cours-Mont-Royal/Communications-Assistant-B--Email-Marketing-_JR0000080349": {
      "title": "Communications Assistant B (Email Marketing)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). University Advancement (UA) promotes McGill to its global community and to the public, engaging alumni, volunteers and friends of the University, and building on McGill’s record of fundraising success in support of University priorities. By joining UA, you can be part of a dynamic and exciting team of professionals that is making an extraordinary impact on the world by advancing the philanthropic and engagement ambitions of McGill University. To find out more about UA, please visit us at www.mcgill.ca/advancement/ua-careers . Hiring Unit : University Advancement, Content Strategy Salary: $16.85 + 4% vacation Hours : 15 hours per week Classification : B Start and end date of employment : contract until January 2, 2027 ***POSITION ONLY AVAILABLE TO CURRENT MCGILL UNDERGRADUATE STUDENTS.*** Job Summary Under the direction of the immediate supervisor, the Communications Assistant (Email Marketing) supports the administration and delivery of email marketing communications for McGill Alumni and donor engagement initiatives. The incumbent assists with managing the email broadcast calendar, building and testing email communications, preparing audience segments, maintaining marketing automation processes, tracking campaign performance, and providing support to system users. The position also contributes to training resources, troubleshooting activities, and the ongoing enhancement of email marketing operations and communications effectiveness. Typical Functions Assist in managing our broadcast calendar and broadcast request queue Assist in building, reviewing and testing emails for various campaigns and communications Assist with audience segmentation and data selection in our CRM (Iris) according to established campaign requirements and specifications Assist with the setup, testing, and maintenance of email automation journeys and data extensions in Salesforce Marketing Cloud Track email performance data and contribute to regular reporting Assist in building marketing journeys for key campaigns Assist in training and troubleshooting support for broadcast users Update and maintain training documentation as needed The list of functions outlined above is representative and not a complete and detailed list of tasks which may be performed by an incumbent. For example, incumbents may be asked to perform some elements of Communications Assistant level \"\"A\"\" tasks in addition to the above listed functions. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities Current McGill student with an interest in communications, marketing, digital media, business, information systems, or a related field.  Strong attention to detail and organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines simultaneously. Experience using digital communication tools, databases, CRM systems, or email marketing platforms; experience with Salesforce Marketing Cloud is considered an asset. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to review content, prepare documentation, and communicate effectively with stakeholders. Demonstrated analytical skills and proficiency working with data, including the ability to track performance metrics, compile reports, and support audience segmentation activities. Knowledge of French is an asset Current McGill undergraduate student Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level 4 on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma 1 Year Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE B) $16.85 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 15 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-09-08 Position End Date: 2027-01-02 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-20 This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Les-Cours-Mont-Royal/Communications-Assistant-B--Social-Media-_JR0000080348": {
      "title": "Communications Assistant B (Social Media)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). University Advancement (UA) promotes McGill to its global community and to the public, engaging alumni, volunteers and friends of the University, and building on McGill’s record of fundraising success in support of University priorities. By joining UA, you can be part of a dynamic and exciting team of professionals that is making an extraordinary impact on the world by advancing the philanthropic and engagement ambitions of McGill University. To find out more about UA, please visit us at www.mcgill.ca/advancement/ua-careers . Hiring Unit : University Advancement, Content Strategy Salary: $16.85 + 4% vacation Hours : 10 hours per week Classification : B Start and end date of employment : contract until January 2, 2027 ***POSITION ONLY AVAILABLE TO CURRENT MCGILL UNDERGRADUATE STUDENTS.*** Job Summary Under the direction of the immediate supervisor (Digital Communications Officer – Social Media), the incumbent supports the planning, creation, scheduling, and evaluation of social media content across McGill Alumni digital channels. The incumbent assists with content production, including photography, video, copywriting, and on-camera appearances, while helping to maintain the social media calendar, monitor platform performance, compile analytics, and promote engagement with students, alumni, faculty, and donors. The incumbent performs functions of moderate complexity using established instructions and procedures. Typical Functions Assist in managing our social media calendar and scheduling posts across McGill Alumni channels Act as an on-camera persona to interview and engage with other students, faculty, alumni and donors, helping to position alumni-focused content from the student POV Assist in creating and/or editing content including photos, reels and copy Track social media performance metrics and contribute to regular reporting Coordinate with social media colleagues across the University to amplify McGill Alumni content on faculty channels Contribute ideas for innovative approaches to content creation across McGill Alumni communications vehicles The list of functions outlined above is representative and not a complete and detailed list of tasks which may be performed by an incumbent. For example, incumbents may be asked to perform some elements of Communications Assistant level \"\"A\"\" tasks in addition to the above listed functions. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities Current McGill student with an interest in communications, marketing, digital media, journalism, or a related field. Experience using social media platforms such as Instagram, LinkedIn, Facebook for content creation and engagement. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to create compelling and audience-focused content. Proficiency with basic photo, video, and graphic editing tools, and an aptitude for learning new digital communications technologies Strong organizational and interpersonal skills, with the ability to manage multiple tasks, collaborate effectively with stakeholders, and work independently when required. French language proficiency is an asset Must be currently enrolled in a Bachelor's Degree at McGill University Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level 4 on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma 1 Year Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE B) $16.85 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 10 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-09-08 Position End Date: 2027-01-02 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-20 This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Sherbrooke-680/Accreditation-and-Quality-Improvement-Officer_JR0000080081": {
      "title": "Accreditation and Quality Improvement Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Reporting to the Director, Administration and Operations, Medical Education, and working in close collaboration with the Associate Dean, PGME, Assistant Dean, Accreditation, and other academic and administrative leaders, the Accreditation and Quality Improvement Officer provides project management and expert support for Postgraduate Medical Education (PGME) accreditation and quality improvement activities. Responsibilities may extend to other Medical Education Programs (UGME and CPD) as required. Role and responsibilities: 1. Develops and maintains expert level of knowledge of relevant accreditation standards. Interprets standards and elements to stakeholders within the Faculty of Medicine Builds and maintains collaborative, productive working relationships with relevant accreditation and physician organizations: ex. the Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada (RCPSC), the College of Family Physicians of Canada (CFPC), and the Collège des médecins du Québec (CMQ) to ensure a nuanced understanding of accreditation requirements and processes Works in collaboration with academic leads and other stakeholders to interpret and define new accreditation requirements Keeps abreast of all process updates and new product developments in accreditation. 2. Manages functioning of and participates in accreditation committees Organizes the collection of accreditation elements for committee review Organizes, assesses, and reports complex, detailed information required for review by relevant accreditation committee(s). Sets up and attends all meetings. Communicates outcomes of the committees to the appropriate stakeholders to generate support for activities related to committee decisions Monitor completion of committee members actions items 3. Manages the acquisition, review, and submission of accreditation reports to accrediting bodies Organizes the completion of: A) the CanAMS instrument for the PGME Institutional Questionnaire and B) the CanAMS instrument for the PGME program questionnaires, C) and any other accreditation or quality improvement related documentation as required Organizes the submission of reports to accrediting bodies, meeting given deadlines Works in close collaboration with academic and administrative leaders in administering the preparation of comprehensive and high-quality self-study reports and progress reports, as necessary Identifies and flags potential threats to accreditation compliance to accreditation Verifies the completeness of report and communication submission and communicates to accrediting bodies Proofreads documents and validates that narrative responses submitted by stakeholders meet the required accreditation standards. Provides feedback on documents and responses to stakeholders, as appropriate. 4. Working in close collaboration with academic leads, documents and follows up on actions required to address the mandatory areas for improvement generated from program accreditation reviews. Oversees the development of action plans at the program and institution level to address gaps identified in accreditation reviews; Supports processes to monitor the implementation of action plans on an ongoing basis. 5. Anticipates and plans annual accreditation-related activities based on accreditation cycle and requirements. Oversees all accreditation activities related to internal or external reviews Organizes the organization of meetings, workshops, training sessions, and other events as required. Manages related budgets and reconcile accounts. Acts as a resource person and advisor to faculty and staff on requirements and priorities. Interprets accreditation-related standards, policies, processes, and procedures Responds to inquiries and provides advice to faculty and staff. Communicates with appropriate stakeholders to ensure that quality improvement action plans are implemented Collaborates with data analyst team to ensure that data is collected and documented according to all accreditation standards for Medicine. 6. Facilitates new ‘site’ accreditation for new learning sites. Guides programs through application process for new programs and for site visits as per PGME policies 7. Supervises administrative staff. Establishes workflows, goals, timelines, and deliverables. Provides support and guidance Assess performance, provide feedback etc. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities Proven results-oriented project management experience, with an established track record of overseeing complex multi-stakeholder workflows and meeting strict timelines. Exceptional organizational and priority-setting skills, with a high level of autonomy and the ability to manage overlapping milestones under pressure. Advanced written and verbal communication skills, specifically a sophisticated ability to draft, proofread, and edit formal institutional documentation. Demonstrated ability to synthesize complex, high-volume qualitative and quantitative data into concise, cohesive narrative reports and strategic presentations. Outstanding diplomatic, interpersonal, and consultation skills, with the demonstrated capacity to foster collaboration, cultivate consensus, and navigate sensitive dynamics. Outstanding organizational skills with strong attention to detail. Bilingual (Written and spoken). Experience in accreditation, quality assurance, or compliance role, especially in an education or healthcare setting considered a strong asset. As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # 4 on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: Bachelor's Degree 3 Years Related Experience / Annual Salary: (MPEX Grade 04) $66,190.00 - $82,740.00 - $99,290.00 Job Profile: MPEX-ADM2A - General Administration - Professional 2 Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Director Administration Position End Date (If applicable): Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-19 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McLennan-Library/Academic-Quality-Assurance-Manager_JR0000079908": {
      "title": "Academic Quality Assurance Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Summary Reporting to the Director, Operations and Academic Programs within Teaching and Academic Programs, the Academic Quality Assurance Manager is responsible for managing and advancing institutional academic quality assurance activities at McGill University. The position provides leadership and expertise in the administration of academic review and accreditation processes, ensuring alignment with University priorities, applicable regulations, and external quality assurance requirements. The role serves as a central resource and liaison for faculties, academic units, senior academic leaders, and governance bodies in matters related to academic quality assurance, accreditation, and academic program planning. The position promotes an integrated and service-oriented approach to academic quality assurance by fostering collaboration across academic and administrative units and by aligning review, accreditation, planning, and continuous improvement activities. Responsibilities Academic reviews and quality assurance management Manage the University's annual academic review process from planning through follow-up and implementation. Ensure academic reviews are conducted in accordance with University policies, governance requirements, and mandated standards. Develop, maintain, and continuously improve academic review procedures, templates, guidance materials, schedules, and supporting documentation. Advise faculties, departments, schools, and review committees on review requirements, timelines, expectations, and best practices. Oversee the preparation, review, and submission of review documentation and dossiers. Monitor institutional compliance with academic quality assurance requirements and identify opportunities for process improvement. Prepare analyses, briefing materials, reports, presentations, and recommendations for senior academic leaders and University committees. Support governance processes associated with academic quality assurance activities. Maintain institutional records and documentation related to academic reviews and quality assurance activities. Accreditation management and support Serve as the central institutional resource for accreditation activities across faculties and academic units. Establish and maintain productive relationships with Faculty accreditation leads and relevant administrative partners. Promote alignment between accreditation processes and institutional academic review requirements to reduce duplication and enhance effectiveness. Provide guidance, tools, and frameworks that support accreditation planning, preparation, implementation, and follow-up activities. Monitor accreditation cycles, requirements, outcomes, and recommendations to identify institutional trends and opportunities for continuous improvement. Compile and analyse accreditation-related information and prepare institutional reports and summaries for senior leadership. Facilitate the exchange of best practices across Faculties, Schools, and programs. Integrated academic planning and continuous improvement Promote the integration of academic quality assurance activities with broader academic program planning, strategic priorities, enrolment considerations, and continuous improvement initiatives of Teaching and Academic Programs (TAP) Conduct research, environmental scans, and analyses related to quality assurance, accreditation, and academic planning trends. Develop performance indicators, tracking mechanisms, and reporting tools that support institutional quality assurance objectives. Identify emerging issues, risks, opportunities, and regulatory developments affecting academic quality assurance. Contribute to the development and implementation of institutional initiatives that enhance academic quality, program effectiveness, and continuous improvement. Support senior academic leaders in the interpretation and application of quality assurance findings to planning and decision-making. Relationship management and service delivery Build and maintain effective working relationships with senior academic leaders, faculty administrators, academic units, governance committees, and external partners (BCI, CVEP). Serve as subject matter expert on academic quality assurance policies, processes, requirements, and best practices. Facilitate meetings, working groups, and consultations related to academic quality assurance, accreditation, and planning initiatives. Promote a collaborative, service-oriented approach that supports Faculties and units’ success while advancing institutional objectives. Education and Experience Undergraduate degree required; graduate degree preferred. French and English, both spoken and written. Minimum three to five years of relevant experience in higher education administration, academic quality assurance, accreditation, institutional planning, governance, program evaluation or development, or a related field. Strong knowledge of University governance, academic program administration, and quality assurance principles. Experience coordinating complex projects involving multiple stakeholders. Experience interpreting policies, regulations, standards, and procedural requirements. Demonstrated analytical, organizational, and communication skills. Competencies Academic quality assurance expertise Project and process management Policy interpretation and implementation Strategic and analytical thinking Relationship management and collaboration Written and oral communication Facilitation and stakeholder engagement Continuous improvement mindset Service orientation Judgment and problem-solving As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: Bachelor's Degree 3 Years Related Experience / Annual Salary: (MPEX Grade 05) $73,470.00 - $91,840.00 - $110,210.00 Job Profile: MPEX-ADM2B - Research Administration - Professional 2 Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Director (Operations and Academic Programs) Position End Date (If applicable): Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-18 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Burnside-Hall/Student-Recruitment-Officer_JR0000079982": {
      "title": "Student Recruitment Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Faculty of Science Geography and Earth Systems (AOS and EPS) This position is a two (2) year term. Position Summary: Are you passionate about science communication and connecting with future students? Under the direction of the Associate Director, Organizational and Cultural Transformation, the Student Recruitment Officer (SRO) plays a key role for the recruitment of prospective students for programs offered in the Departments of Atmospheric and Oceanic Sciences (AOS), Earth and Planetary Sciences (EPS), and Geography, within the Faculty of Science. The SRO will work in close collaboration with the Area manager and their administrative team. The SRO will participate in the development and implementation of recruitment plans and marketing initiatives to promote programs and increase student enrollment. This includes representing the departments at various events, hosting student visitors, building an online presence, developing relationships with internal units and external organizations and evaluating various recruitment efforts. Primary Responsibilities: Oversee the planning, development, and implementation of recruitment plans to promote programs and maximize student enrollment in the Departments of AOS, EPS, and Geography. Participate in in-person and virtual recruitment activities and events within the province of Quebec and Ontario (McGill Open House, orientation, site visits to anglophone and francophone CEGEPs and Secondary Schools, etc.) and represent the departments. Build and deliver engaging presentations, in English and in French, to prospective students and their parents to raise awareness and advise on programs, prerequisites and admissions. Provide clear guidance concerning on-campus services, student life, tuition, financial assistance, potential career paths, etc. Host student groups from schools and CEGEPs visiting the departments and develop workshops and activities to enhance their visits and experience. Collaborate and develop effective working relationships with the Faculty of Science and McGill units that provide student and recruitment-related services. Maintain regular contact with schools and CEGEPs in order to promote programs and revisions, special events, offerings, etc. Maintain databases to track contacts and activities (e.g. schools, contact details, names of counsellors, record of institutions visited relative to “yield” statistics, etc.).  Event Planning and Logistics Manage all logistical arrangements for recruitment activities and events and organize for presence/participation/demonstration of current students at events when possible. Prepare practical information for visits (level of interest, type of booth for event type, information format, etc.) Marketing and Communications Develop compelling marketing materials and promotional content for recruitment activities and events, branding and communications. This includes flyers, newsletters, brochures, posters, etc. Build a social media plan and oversee online presence on platforms (Facebook, Instagram, X/Twitter, LinkedIn etc.). Manage department websites and customize content to targeted audiences to increase student engagement and enrollment. Other Analyze admissions data to identify priority student groups and design targeted outreach initiatives that promote enrollment in specific departments. Prepare reports of recruitment activities, including analysis of engagement metrics, event outcomes, and recommendations for future outreach. Provide support with graduation-related activities, as required. Undertake special projects based on departmental priorities. Note : The incumbent may work evenings and weekends for open house and other events. Your Qualifications: Education : Undergraduate degree in a Science field is an asset. Experience : Student recruitment and outreach experience, in a higher education setting is preferred. Your Key Strengths: Bilingual; excellent verbal and written communication skills, in both English and French. Demonstrated experience with the development and implementation of student recruitment activities. Passion for science communication and youth engagement. Proven experience advising potential students on admission requirements. Exceptional interpersonal skills, both for internal and external relations, including tact, diplomacy, discretion and good judgment. Experience organizing and planning recruitment-related events locally and off-campus. Strong experience in public speaking tailored to different audiences (adult, CEGEP and/or Secondary School students, etc.). Ability to translate complex concepts into accessible, inspiring stories for younger audiences. Detail-oriented, organized and autonomous with the ability to prioritize, multitask, and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Client–focused and service-oriented self-starter with strong problem-solving and decision-making skills. Proven interpersonal skills with a strong sense of professionalism, and ability to build constructive and effective relationships in an academic setting. Proficient using MS Office Suite (Word, PowerPoint, Outlook and Excel), as well as, web, content management and social media tools and platforms (e.g., Drupal, WordPress, Instagram, X, LinkedIn, etc.).  As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level #4(qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: Bachelor's Degree 3 Years Related Experience / Annual Salary: (MPEX Grade 04) $66,190.00 - $82,740.00 - $99,290.00 Job Profile: MPEX-SAF2A - Student Enrolment - Professional 2 Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Associate Director, Organizational and Cultural Transformation Position End Date (If applicable): 2028-08-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-18 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Sherbrooke-680/Administrative-Coordinator_JR0000080249": {
      "title": "Administrative Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary: Under the direction of the immediate supervisor, provides administrative and secretarial support. Participates in ensuring the smooth functioning of the unit’s operations. Acts as resource person for policies and procedures. Administers unit accounts. Assists in the organization of unit activities. Responsible for documents and files of the unit. Maintains computerized information systems. Major Duties and Responsibilities: Acts as a frontline resource person regarding the ASC’s policies and procedures related to finance and human resources. Resolves problems within area of responsibility. Consults relevant documentation and liaises with appropriate resource persons to obtain and provide information on diverse and complex issues. Participates in ensuring the smooth functioning of the ASC. Recommends procedural changes to enable ASC to function more effectively. Collaborates with manager and others in establishing work priorities. Follows up on and ensures appropriate implementation of decisions made by manager. Processes payments through MMP - specifically paying invoices/requisitions for vendors, handles all financial transactions, etc.  Keeps records of all payments, summer course activity fees (Chinese and Japanese) reconciliation, etc. Submits expense reports for speakers, recruitment, summer course lecturers. Reviews expense reports prior to submission of expense reports to the FST; brings any issues to the attention of the Administrative Supervisor. In consultation with Administrative Supervisor, initiates journal transfers and maintains inventory of funds that need to be transferred in or out of the Unit. Assists Administrative Supervisor with research grant administration. Assists Administrative Supervisor with academic recruitment (advertisement, hotel, scheduling of interviews, etc.). Provides assistance to researchers with preparing fund approval forms, and begins job requisitions in Workday, for Research Assistants appointments. Is the timekeeper for graders, RAs and any other employee who submits hours on Workday.  Follows-up with Professors re. Workday approvals, renewal/termination of appointments, and ensures that funding is available.  Coordinates travel arrangements, schedules Speaker Series/ guest lecturers for the units. Assists with the administration of some research funds - pays invoices, reconciles financial statements and requests yearly financial statements as required.  Follows-up on financial transaction issues and ensures that Administrative Supervisor is kept up-to-date on these issues. In accordance with established policies and procedures, prepares financial payments of a routine nature for staff Requests yearly financial statements, if needed keeps records, inputs and verifies data pertaining payments. Assists with the organization and preparation of the Seminar Series and other events as required. Makes all arrangements relating to publicity, accommodation, schedule, and budget. Under the direction of the Administrative Supervisor, provides secretarial and administrative support for the academic/administrative activities of the Units. Coordinates the administrative activities of the Units. Provides day to day administrative support to the Administrative Supervisor which includes the writing, editing and proofreading of the manager’s routine correspondence relating to the Faculty/University or external units. Assists with the preparation of documentation and background material, which includes transcribing Department Meeting Minutes.   Also provides administrative support to the Student Affairs Team. Assists with daily office operations, as well as tracking keys, creating mailboxes, assisting course lecturers with office space, archiving material, etc.  Updates the websites for East Asian Studies and Languages, Literatures, and Cultures.  Liaises with Academics regarding course syllabi, office hours, etc. The list of duties and responsibilities outlined above is representative and not a complete and detailed list of tasks which may be performed by an employee whose position has been matched to this generic job description. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities: Experience in a frontline position serving cross-cultural customers and stakeholders. Experience providing administrative support in an office environment. Experience working in an educational setting, an asset. Excellent organizational skills and proven ability to multi-task in a team-oriented environment. Must possess strong customer focus and service-oriented skills. Excellent communication skills with a proven ability to clearly and effectively receive, retain and transmit information at all levels. Proven ability to work in a PC environment using word-processing, spreadsheets, databases, presentation software, email, Minerva and Banner (FIS, SIS). English and French, spoken and written. As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level 4 (fluent) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: DEP - Secretarial Studies 4 Years Related Experience / DEP - Office Systems Hourly Salary: (MUNACA Level F) $29.42 - $36.46 Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Administrative Supervisor Position End Date (If applicable): Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-19 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Strathcona-Music/Customer-Services-Coordinator_JR0000080092": {
      "title": "Customer Services Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary: Under the direction of the immediate supervisor, coordinates customer service. Organizes, distributes and verifies the work of others and participates in their training. Acts as resource person. Deals with customer requests, enquiries and complaints. Orders parts and equipment, controls inventory, and maintains computerized information systems. Performs administrative and accounting tasks appropriate to the activities of the unit. Major Duties and Responsibilities: Trains, organizes, distributes and verifies the work of one regular support staff and casuals. Establishes priorities. Acts as resource person for the day-to day operations of the Building Services department. Trouble-shoots and resolves complex problems. Verifies the work of external contractors as this relates to Building Services for the Schulich School of Music. Sets priorities to efficiently and effectively provide prompt and accurate response to clients’ needs which are conveyed by phone, by email and in person. Explains and confirms that all policies and procedures are followed to ensure the security of equipment and instrument inventory. Inspects rentals upon return and determines need for and coordinates servicing, repair and/or replacements; makes recommendations to supervisor. Follows up to ensure timely return of equipment and instruments. Administers fines and repair/replacement costs. Verifies equipment and instruments upon return from repair and ensures conformity. Reviews relevant invoices and follows-up on discrepanicies. Maintains inventory of loans of temporary and permanent keys for all Schulich School of Music buildings; orders replacements and/or lock changes for lost keys. Receives loan payments and makes reimbursements. Coordinates lock re-pinning. Maintains Lenel card inventory and updates database to ensure users have access to necessary locations. Makes purchases of related supplies as necessary.   Ensures adequate supply of First Aid supplies and replenishes as needed. Liaises and or collaborates regularly with several internal and external departments/consultants such as Maintenance, Facilities Mgmt., Cleaners, Security, Fire Safety Office, Electricians, Elevator repair service, Archivex. Recycling and Garbage Collection services, Locksmiths and Lenel technicians. Receives, prioritizes and schedules bookings for conference and practice rooms. Modifies schedules as necessary and informs parties involved of changes. Coordinates follow-up and cleaning and furniture moves as required. Maintains various electronic and manual files; utilizes various software programs such as FORS, Maximo, Lenel, RBS, Access, Excel, Outlook, Minerva and Word. Assist   with permanent and ad hoc room bookings   Answer general email and walk-in inquiries; Act as first point of contact for Building Office and the Schulich School of Music information desk, as needed.   Assist   with moving furniture and updating building inventory as   required   Performs other duties as required. The list of duties and responsibilities outlined above is representative and not a complete and detailed list of tasks which may be performed by an employee whose position has been matched to this generic job description. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities: Strong knowledge of Music Faculty operations and booking system   Fully bilingual (English and French, written and spoken)   Extensive knowledge of musical instruments essential   Detail-oriented with strong organizational skills   Excellent time-management skills and ability to work in a fast-paced environment   As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: DEP - Office Systems 3 Years Related Experience / Hourly Salary: (MUNACA Level F) $29.42 - $36.46 Hours per Week: 20.25 (Part time) Monday, Tuesday, Thursday Supervisor: Manager Administration Position End Date (If applicable): 2027-06-18 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-18 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McIntyre--Medical/Research-Assistant-2_JR0000080343": {
      "title": "Research Assistant 2",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Prof. Arnim Pause's Lab - Rosalind and Morris Goodman Cancer Institute Supervisor: Prof. Arnim Pause Position Summary: The candidate will be responsible for: Taking care of the animal colony and genotyping of all the animal models housed by the lab. Participate in any animal surgeries and procedures conducted by lab members. Maintain cell lines in culture and conduct cell line-based experiments such as: WB, RT-qPCR and others. Contribute to general lab-manager duties, such as keeping lab records up to date and jointly with Prof Arnim Pause manage lab's finances. Perform molecular biology techniques including plasmid cloning, lentiviral construct design, and transformation/transfection for generating stable and inducible cell lines. Conduct immunofluorescence, immunohistochemistry (IHC), and confocal microscopy imaging to characterize tumor and organoid phenotypes. Assist with tumor and tissue processing (FFPE and frozen sections) and downstream histological analysis. Educational Qualifications: Possesses specialized knowledge of the field or discipline acquired through a Master’s Degree in the relevant field. Additional Skills & Qualifications: Properly trained on animal work, including handling, husbandry, and procedures sufficient to independently manage the lab's mouse colony. Already familiar with the lab's core techniques and ongoing projects, allowing for a shortened onboarding/training period. Experience with molecular cloning, lentiviral construct design, and generation of stable/inducible cell lines. Proficient in standard cell and molecular biology techniques (western blotting, RT-qPCR, immunofluorescence/IHC). Knowledge of French and English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level #4 (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4. This position is covered by the Association of McGill University Research Employees (AMURE) collective agreement. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $34.65 Hours per Week: 40 (Full time) Location: McIntyre Medical Supervisor: Professor Position Start Date: 2026-09-28 Position End Date: 2027-06-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-14 This position is covered by the Association of McGill University Research Employees (AMURE) collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
