    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Strathcona-Music/Office-Assistant-C--Graduate-Studies---Schulich-_JR0000080709": {
      "title": "Office Assistant C (Graduate Studies - Schulich)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Student Services - Schulich School of Music Position Summary: Under the direction of the Manager of Student Services, Schulich School of Music, the incumbent may perform some or all of the listed general administration functions. These functions are of high complexity, and the incumbent performs them using general instruction. Key Responsibilities: Front counter coverage, respond to general enquiries Assist in organizing and scheduling Comprehensive Exams, general exams and Exam Recitals for graduate students Follow up with examiners regarding assessment and evaluation Collects data and prepare entries for payroll Prepares letters for approval (could be for scholarships, immigration papers, etc).  Assists with the follow-up of missing documents from students.   Email correspondence, respond to enquiries, follows up as needed Direct graduate students to appropriate resources Prepare files for archives Other duties related to Graduate Studies Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities Dynamic and enthusiastic with strong interpersonal skills. Good communication in person and via email. Demonstrated organizational skills and strong attention to detail. Enjoys working independently and as part of a team. In-depth knowledge of music and instrumental/vocal ensembles. Knowledge of the McGill University, Schulich School of Music graduate programs is an asset. Knowledge of Microsoft Word, Excel. Basic French is an asset. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # 4 (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma 2 Years Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE C) $17.17 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 15 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-10-01 Position End Date: 2026-11-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-23 This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Sherbrooke-680/TA--Fall-2026--Applied-Health-and-Physical-Assessment-Anatomy-1-NUR1-338-001_JR0000080711": {
      "title": "TA  Fall 2026: Applied Health and Physical Assessment/Anatomy 1-NUR1 338 001",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Ingram School of Nursing Course Title: Applied Health and Physical Assessment/Anatomy Course Code: NUR1 338 005 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 90 Hiring Unit: Ingram School of Nursing Course Title and Course Number: Applied Health and Physical Assessment/Anatomy 1- NUR1 338 001 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 90 hours per position Dates: September 21, 2026 to December 22, 2026 Job Description: Under the supervision of the course coordinator, the Teaching Assistant (TA) supports the delivery of the Health and Physical Assessment course for nursing students. This includes reviewing course content, assisting with student learning, participating in evaluation activities, participating in anatomy labs and helping implement the course plan. TAs are available to answer student questions, may assist during office hours or review sessions, and contribute to a positive and supportive learning environment. Mix of synchronous and asynchronous work. Salary: $38.46/hour Desired Major(s): Nursing Desired Degree Level:   Masters & Grad Dips & Certs Qualifications: Applicants must have successfully completed Health and Physical Assessment courses (NUR1 338/339 or NUR1 235/236 or NUR2 534/535). Masters or Doctoral student at McGill. Prior experience as a Teaching Assistant for NUR1 338, NUR1 339, or NUR1 235, NUR1 236 or NUR2 534, NUR2 535 is preferred. Graduate teaching experience is an asset. Bilingualism in French and English is an asset. Must be legally eligible to work in Canada. McGill University is Committed to Equity in Employment. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2026-09-21 Position End Date: 2026-12-22 Deadline to Apply: McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Brown-Student-Serv/Associate-Director-Administration_JR0000080391": {
      "title": "Associate Director Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Office of the Senior Director Student Services (OS2) McGill Student Services is composed of seven specialties providing a wide range of services to students, including health, mental health, financial, career, disability accommodation, religious and spiritual life, transition to and from university, as well as services specific to international students. The Office of the Senior Director provides strategic leadership, operational and infrastructure excellence, and integrated communications in support of Student Services. Bringing together expertise in administration, finance, human resources, project management, communications and student engagement, OS2 enables the delivery of high-quality services and programming that enhance the student experience, and support student success and well-being. Position Summary Reporting to the Senior Director of Student Services, the Associate Director, Administration is responsible for strategic resource planning and reporting across the Student Services portfolio, oversight to ensure alignment of budget development, forecasting, workforce planning, and coordinated provision of human resources and finance services. Acts as a key advisor to the Senior Director and service leaders on financial and workforce planning and performance, operational efficiency, and risk management. Additionally, this individual will act as an agent of change, driving improvements and innovation across  operational functions to enhance effectiveness and support the evolving needs of Student Services. Primary Responsibilities Provides strategic leadership in operations and resource oversight including human resources and financial management, ensuring compliance with policies and promoting a culture of collaboration and service excellence Supports the Senior Director and leadership team with business insight to help shape strategy and create long-term value. Oversees business alignment with multi-year resource planning, as well as annual budget and workforce development, including scenario planning, forecasting, risk analysis and performance reporting.  Ensure adherence to  stewardship obligations. Lead the Finance and Human Resources specialists for coordinated  support of each of seven Student Service units, with full understanding of unique business needs and specificities, and collaboration with different stakeholders across the university. Oversee major contractual and procurement activities in partnership with Procurement Services, ensuring compliance and cost-effectiveness. Oversee Medical Billing services across multiple insurance plans (private and public) in support of the Student Wellness Hub physicians, psychiatrists and laboratory services. Develop and maintain inventory of system assets and oversee IT project prioritization plan as determined by Student Services leadership.  Collaborate with IT Services to manage system access protocols, as well as inventory and optimize technology resources within budget constraints. Develop real-time analytics for data-driven decision making. Implement and maintain a reporting strategy for monitoring and identification of financial risks and opportunities throughout the fiscal year.  Plan, develop and oversee processes, procedures, protocols and unit policies in accordance with Office of Student Services goals and objectives; design and implement protocols for internal Knowledge Base, production schedule and user manuals for all Office positions. Develop and maintain strategy for record management and act as resource to services in regards to record retention, privacy and access to information laws and policies. Drive operational efficiency and cost-saving initiatives through lean, clear and transparent processes, and consideration of internal controls to assist with strong governance and stewardship of resources. Conduct cost-benefit analyses and ensure financial compliance in all initiatives. Provide senior professional expertise and strategic  advice to the Senior Director of Student Services, resolving any difficulties as needed.  Primary stakeholders include Office of Associate Provost Student Life & Learning, University Advancement, IT, Financial Services and Student Accounts Serve as a contributing member of the Student Services Leadership Team. Lead change management initiatives to improve financial, HR, and operational processes, fostering a culture of continuous improvement and innovation. Attract, develop, and retain high-performing staff within the Finance, Medical Billing and HR specialities. Other Qualifying Skills and Abilities Strong planning, analytical and financial management skills. Ability to synthesize data and develop cohesive financial strategies and multi-year plans. Experience with project implementation and management, including system deployments. Proven client service excellence Demonstrated ability to act as a change agent, driving process improvements and organizational transformation. Strong leadership in change management and stakeholder engagement. Excellent communication and presentation skills. Proficiency with Banner FIS, Workday, budgeting tools, and reporting software. Knowledge of university operations, procurement, and payroll processes. Bilingual: English (spoken and written), French (spoken and read). Knowledge of French and English: McGill University is an English-language university where day-to-day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level #4-Fluent on a scale of 0-4.  Minimum Education and Experience: Bachelor's Degree 5 Years Related Experience / Annual Salary: (MPEX Grade 07) $92,150.00 - $115,190.00 - $138,230.00 Job Profile: MPEX-ADM3A - General Administration - Senior Professional/Manager Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Senior Director Student Services Position End Date (If applicable): Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-02 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Bronfman-Building/CTAQ-Research-Associate_JR0000080828": {
      "title": "CTAQ Research Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary: Research Associate needed to conduct a literature review, participate in the development of research tools, conduct individual interviews with partners and consumers, perform statistical analyses. Qualifications: We need a research associate (a PhD student or already with a doctoral degree), in marketing/ management, nutrition, health sciences or equivalent. Knowledge of French and English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # 4 on a scale of 0-4 Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $35.37 Hours per Week: 10 (Part time) Location: Bronfman Building Supervisor: Assistant Professor Position Start Date: 2026-06-15 Position End Date: 2026-09-25 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-23 This position is covered by the Association of McGill University Research Employees (AMURE) collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McLennan-Library/Senior-Student-Ambassador_JR0000080816": {
      "title": "Senior Student Ambassador",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary: Under the direction of the immediate supervisor, the incumbent may perform some or all of the listed general administration functions. These functions are of high complexity and the incumbent performs them using general instruction. Duties and Responsibilities: Reviews and updates the tour scripts. Hosts virtual and in-person campus tours to the public, VIP guests (country delegates, government officials, donors, etc.). Trains and evaluates the work of the student ambassadors. Represents McGill as the first point of contact at the Welcome Centre. Greets and advises prospective students on the University (programs, admissions (all pools), legal documents, campus life, tuition, Montreal life, etc.) with a knowledgeable and positive attitude. Provides administrative support at the Welcome Centre by answering phones, responding to e-mails, and assisting in various administrative tasks. Using technology and software to perform duties and responsibilities. Provide administrative support of recruitment activities and events (set up and take down of signs, manage kiosk, provide written feedback on event, equipment and furniture, data entry, etc.). Conducts research via social media and internet searches. Participates in social media campaigns and events (ex. Instagram, Facebook and YouTube). Some video and photo editing may be required. The list of functions outlined above is representative and not a complete and detailed list of tasks which may be performed by an incumbent. For example, incumbent may be asked to perform some elements of Communications Assistant level “A” and/or “B” in addition to the above listed functions. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities: Experience as a student ambassador. General knowledge of the downtown campus and student life. Strong written and oral communication skills. Strong interpersonal skills - must be outgoing, willing to engage and initiate conversations with students and their families / able to adapt quickly to situations (ex: construction on campus). Extremely reliable and punctual. Involvement in the McGill community (clubs, services, athletics, or other university activities) an asset. Customer service and social media experience an asset. Hiring Unit: Admissions and Recruitment Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma 2 Years Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE C) $18.00 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 20 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-09-18 Position End Date: 2027-04-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-24 This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
