    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Montreal-Neuro/Research-Associate_JR0000080567": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). The Laboratory of Professor Etienne De Villers-Sidani is seeking a highly motivated and qualified Research Associate to join its team. The laboratory develops digital biomarkers of brain function derived from eye-tracking and speech/voice recordings, with the goal of detecting and monitoring neurological disorders (e.g., neurodegenerative, neuroimmunological and neuromuscular diseases). Reporting to the principal investigator, the incumbent will act as the lab's data scientist: designing, implementing and validating algorithms on multimodal clinical datasets, and independently writing up and communicating the results in the scientific literature. Main responsibilities •       Design, implement and optimize signal-processing, statistical and machine-learning algorithms for eye-movement (oculomotor) and voice/speech data. •       Validate algorithms against clinical reference standards: accuracy, reliability (test–retest), longitudinal sensitivity to change, and generalizability across cohorts. •       Curate, quality-control and analyze large multimodal clinical datasets; maintain reproducible, documented analysis pipelines and code. •       Draft peer-reviewed scientific articles with a high degree of autonomy (from analysis plan to submission and response to reviewers), as well as abstracts, reports and grant sections. •       Present findings at lab meetings and scientific conferences, and communicate effectively with clinicians, engineers, trainees and local, national and international collaborators. Required qualifications Education:  PhD in computer science, engineering, mathematics/statistics, computational neuroscience or a related quantitative discipline. C omputing:  Advanced programming skills (e.g., Python and/or R, MATLAB; scientific and ML libraries), with sound software practices (version control, reproducible pipelines). Mathematics:  Strong mathematical and statistical background (signal processing, time-series analysis, machine learning, mixed-effects/longitudinal models, diagnostic-accuracy statistics). Scientific writing:  Demonstrated ability to write scientific articles autonomously, evidenced by a first-author publication record. Communication and autonomy:  Ability to work independently, manage several projects in parallel and communicate complex results clearly to multidisciplinary audiences. Assets •       Experience with eye-tracking, speech/audio or other physiological or biomedical signals. •       Experience with clinical or health research data. •       Knowledge of neuroscience or neurological disorders. This position is covered by the AMURE collective agreement: http://www.aerum-amure.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/AMURE-2023-2027.pdf Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level 4 on a scale of 0-4. Hourly Salary: $35.37 Hours per Week: 40 (Full time) Location: Montreal Neuro. Supervisor: Associate Professor Position Start Date: 2026-09-28 Position End Date: 2027-03-27 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-23 This position is covered by the Association of McGill University Research Employees (AMURE) collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Montreal-Neuro/Research-Assistant-2_JR0000080746": {
      "title": "Research Assistant 2",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary: The candidate will be responsible for designing and performing experimental procedures aimed at investigating how the dopamine neurons are altered in disease models using in vivo calcium imaging, behavioural analysis, confocal and super-resolution microscopy, drug administration, blood collection, euthanasia and brain/organ collection, etc. To achieve these goals, the candidate will be expected to provide new ideas and suggestions by reading the literature related to this project. Examples of experimental procedures include optimising new circuit labelling approaches, developing novel behavioural paradigms, and generating new transgenic mouse models. The incumbent is expected to quantify, analyze, and present experiment results at lab meetings or in peer-reviewed publications. Based on intellectual contribution, the research assistant will be given the opportunity to be an author on any publication that will derive from the work performed. In addition to performing these experiments, the candidate will be involved in the maintenance of our mouse colony (e.g. breeding, weaning, and genotyping), ordering, and providing technical guidance and training to undergraduate students. Qualifications: Master's Degree This position is covered by the AMURE collective agreement: AMURE-2023-2027.pdf (aerum-amure.ca)   Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level 3 on a scale of 0-4. For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Hourly Salary: $32.15 Hours per Week: 40 (Full time) Location: Montreal Neuro. Supervisor: Associate Professor (Clinical) Position Start Date: 2026-09-28 Position End Date: 2027-09-27 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-24 This position is covered by the Association of McGill University Research Employees (AMURE) collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Brown-Student-Serv/Scholarship-Selections---Outreach-Officer_JR0000080026-1": {
      "title": "Scholarship Selections & Outreach Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). International Student Services International Student Services (ISS) supports the growth, progress, and success of all international students (including visiting and exchange students) at McGill and aims to ease their transition to a new university, a new home and a new country. They provide a range of services and resources for international students including orientation webinars, immigration advising, health insurance guidance, and social and cultural programming and events. Position Summary Reporting to the Program Manager, the MCF Scholarship Selection and Outreach Officer will support the management, implementation, and evaluation of recruitment and yield strategies for selection of the scholars for the Mastercard Foundation Scholars Program at McGill University. This role involves providing high-quality advice and service on a wide range of admissions-related matters to prospective applicants, Program Partners, the public, and senior management. The incumbent will represent the program through virtual and in-person outreach, participate in recruitment events, and collaborate with internal stakeholders to ensure alignment between recruitment strategies, scholarship selection and admissions operations. Major Responsibilities : Attend outreach events, in person across the African continent organized by the Mastercard Foundation and its partners, and virtually to support recruitment goals and priority group targets for the Program. Serve as the primary point of contact for all prospective scholars throughout the admissions process. Determine admission and Scholarship eligibility of applicants, by considering multiple sources of information, based on predetermined guidelines and procedures. Manage the Scholarship Selection Committee and the scholar selection process. Act as the main contact for the scholarship applications software and triage inquiries efficiently. Ensure alignment with Enrolment Services and Graduate Programs Offices. Prepare and deliver engaging information sessions and presentations. Maintain and update the program’s application webpage. Develop and manage communication tools and promotional materials for the Mastercard Foundation Scholars Program at McGill University, namely website and LinkedIn pages) Collaborate with subject matter experts to create targeted resources. Analize market trends and best practices in recruitment and enrolment, especially amongst Mastercard Foundation partners. Participate in working groups, project teams, and committees. Contribute to strategic initiatives aligned with university enrolment priorities. Track recruitment and selection metrics and provide regular reports. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities: Experience designing and facilitating workshops and information sessions, particularly within multicultural settings. Experience working with international students Knowledge of African contexts; experience working in Africa considered an asset. Excellent interpersonal skills and inter-cultural competences. Knowledge of University policies and procedures. Proven ability to prioritize and administer multiple projects simultaneously, work under pressure and meet deadlines in a rapidly changing environment. Demonstrated ability to work independently and as part of a team with minimal direction. Computer literate with all Microsoft Office tools. Experience with Banner (SIS) and Minerva is an asset. Excellent communication skills, written and verbal. Experience leading discussion groups and classes. English and French, spoken and written. Third language is an asset. Knowledge of French and English: McGill University is an English-language university where day-to-day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # 4 (Fluent) on a scale of 0-4.  Minimum Education and Experience: Bachelor's Degree 3 Years Related Experience / Annual Salary: (MPEX Grade 04) $66,190.00 - $82,740.00 - $99,290.00 Job Profile: MPEX-SAF2A - Student Enrolment - Professional 2 Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Program Manager Position End Date (If applicable): 2027-12-01 Deadline to Apply: McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/James-Admin-Bldg/Graphic-Designer_JR0000080823": {
      "title": "Graphic Designer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary: The Graphic Designer plays an important role in supporting McGill University's visual identity, institutional communications, and initiatives. Reporting to the Associate Director, Creative Services, the incumbent develops high-quality visual communications that strengthen McGill's brand, enhance stakeholder engagement, and reinforce the University's reputation. Working closely with senior leadership, academic and administrative units, advancement teams, external partners, and other major institutional clients, the Graphic Designer researches, conceptualizes, designs, and produces impactful print and digital materials that effectively communicate key messages across a variety of platforms and audiences. The incumbent develops and maintains strong client relationships, manages projects of varying scope and complexity, and delivers high-quality design solutions that meet client objectives, timelines, budgets, and brand standards. The role requires the ability to translate complex information into engaging visual communications while balancing creativity, sound design judgement and exceptional client service. Primary Responsibilities: Creative Design & Brand Management Design and produce a wide range of marketing and communications materials, in consultation with the Associate Director, Creative Services, to support the promotion of McGill University to internal and external audiences. Develop design concepts and produce high-quality print and digital materials that align with McGill's brand standards and communication goals. Consult with clients to identify communication objectives, target audiences, project requirements, timelines, and deliverables. Research, analyze, and assess design requirements to develop creative, targeted, and effective visual communication solutions. Translate complex academic, research, and institutional information into clear and engaging visual formats. Collaborate with communications, marketing, advancement, and recruitment teams to develop visual solutions that support institutional priorities. Present creative concepts and recommendations to stakeholders and effectively incorporate feedback into design solutions. Create graphics and visual assets for websites, email campaigns, digital advertising, and social media platforms. Support campaigns related to student recruitment, fundraising, research promotion, alumni engagement, and community outreach. Support multimedia initiatives, including motion graphics and video projects when required. Ensure consistency, accuracy, and quality across all visual communications while maintaining the integrity of the University's visual identity. Optimize designs for accessibility, usability, and digital engagement. Project Management Manage multiple concurrent projects from concept through final delivery. Develop project schedules, budget estimates, obtain approvals, and ensure deadlines are met. Liaise with printers, photographers, videographers, and external vendors as required. Monitor project budgets and production specifications. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities Bachelor's degree or diploma in Graphic Design, Visual Communications, Fine Arts, or a related field. Minimum 5 years of professional graphic design experience, preferably within higher education, government, not-for-profit, or a complex institutional environment. Experience managing projects and relationships with senior stakeholders and high-profile clients. Portfolio demonstrating excellence in print and digital design. Advanced proficiency in Adobe Creative Cloud (InDesign, Illustrator, Photoshop, and Acrobat) Experience with presentation design software (PowerPoint). Knowledge of web and digital design best practices. Familiarity with accessibility standards and inclusive design principles. Exceptional visual design and creative problem-solving skills. Strong client service and relationship management abilities. Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English and French. Ability to translate complex information into engaging visual content. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Attention to detail and commitment to quality. Sound judgment and ability to manage confidential or sensitive projects. External partners, vendors, and community stakeholders As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # 4 on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: Bachelor's Degree 3 Years Related Experience / Annual Salary: (MPEX Grade 04) $66,190.00 - $82,740.00 - $99,290.00 Job Profile: MPEX-COM2A - Internal External Relations - Professional 2 Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Associate Director, Creative Services Position End Date (If applicable): Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-06 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/MUHC-GLEN/Administrative-Coordinator_JR0000078513": {
      "title": "Administrative Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary: Provides high-level administrative and operational support, serving as a key point of contact for the departmental Divisions in the Department of Medicine (DOM). Coordinates scheduling, planning, and implementation of programs and strategic initiatives, while ensuring that administrative services are delivered efficiently and in alignment with departmental goals and priorities. Major Duties and Responsibilities: Support and  coordinate programs, events, and academic initiatives for the McGill Divisions including Grand Rounds, Research Days, and Symposia; oversee logistics, scheduling, and accreditation requirements. Provide administrative support to the McGill Divisions in the department, including coordinating meetings, coordinating schedules, supporting program and event planning, and preparing and distributing meeting documentation and minutes. Support financial operations by processing inter-fund transfers, monitoring accounts, preparing and submitting expense reports, and administering one-time payments (including guest lecturer honoraria) and procurement requests (e.g., MMP). Coordinate the Department of Medicine services to its members by supporting a wide range of operational requests, including the creation and management of research and principal investigator funds, while ensuring timely and accurate responses. Support departmental/divisional communications and outreach by   coordinating newsletter development  and distribution (Envoke), maintaining and updating website content (e.g., Grand Rounds), and sharing communications through social media platforms (Twitter/X). Draft and prepare editorial content , including faculty features, stories, and interview materials. Coordinate the collection, consolidation, and preparation of divisional reports for the Department’s Annual Report, ensuring completeness, accuracy, and adherence to deadlines. Schedules meetings, contacts participants and books meetings venue. Assists with preparation of agenda. Attends meetings, takes minutes, and follows up on decisions within area of responsibility. The list of duties and responsibilities outlined above is representative and not a complete and detailed list of tasks which may be performed by an employee whose position has been matched to this generic job description. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities: Experience with processing expense reports, use of Minerva, and McGill Market Place. Experience with social media management Ability to work autonomously and as part of a team. Demonstrated organizational skills and ability to multi-task. Excellent attention to detail. Excellent judgment, tact and discretion. · Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and other tech tools (survey monkey, Doodle, Copilot) etc. Bilingual in English and French. As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # 4 on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: DEP - Secretarial Studies 4 Years Related Experience / DEP - Office Systems Hourly Salary: (MUNACA Level F) $29.42 - $36.46 Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Administrative Manager Position End Date (If applicable): Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-26 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
