    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Currie-Gymnasium/Sports-Instructor_JR0000079415": {
      "title": "Sports Instructor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-23\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary: Under the direction of the immediate supervisor, the Sports Instructor, will be responsible for planning and leading the designated sport group lessons and private lessons to the registered patrons. The lessons will range from beginner to advanced levels. Primary Responsibilities: Lead designated sport group lessons and private lessons. Adapt lessons for the specific groups - ranging from beginners to advanced. As required, modify moves, and techniques for patrons who may have limitations. Address any emergency issues requiring attention to supervisor or security. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities Strong knowledge in the sport interested in being hire Effective communication, attentiveness and active listening skills Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma 3 Years Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE D) $18.92 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 6 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-08-03 Position End Date: 2027-04-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-06 This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
