    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Duff-Medical-Bldg/Teaching-Assistant---MIMM-314---Intermediate-Immunology-Winter-2027_JR0000080596": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant - MIMM 314 - Intermediate Immunology Winter 2027",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Microbiology & Immunology Course Title: Intermediate Immunology Course Code: MIMM 314 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 90 Position Summary:   Grading short written answers in quizzes and exams according to an outlined format for the answers.  Enter these grades into a spreadsheet. Assist with the uploading of course content on MyCourses ( feel free to change or add to content )   Take questions from students in person or via email and answer them according to a reasonable weekly schedule. Seek help from the lecturer or coordinator in dealing with difficult questions or organizational matters. Visit the students' MyCourses and Facebook discussion groups daily to interject a comment when correction or guidance is necessary. Build a list of frequently asked or instructive questions and answers which can be made available on MyCourses. Arrange and give at least 2 (two) pre-exam tutorial/discussion sessions (if requested) based upon problems students have which the TA has identified in advance. Be ready to lead group discussions during 2 Mystery Cases in class. Be present at lectures sufficiently to allow the students and lecturers to get to know you and become familiar with the professors and their classes. Assist with setup and adjudication of mid-term/finals exams. In cooperation with the coordinator, be present at the mid-term exam in case of problems and student questions. Meet with the coordinator periodically to discuss the progress of the course in relation to the TA work schedule, and to the institute changes or innovations to improve the communication and learning process.     Qualifications:   Preferably knowledge of Immunology & Microbiology and key research methods and ideally having taken at least the Immunology MIMM 214 and 314 coursed, or a substantially equivalent Immunology course, and performed well in it. Excellent time management skills are required.   Language Requirements (if relevant):    Effective communication skills in English are essential. An effective communication skill in French is desirable.   Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2027-01-05 Position End Date: 2027-04-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-01 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Duff-Medical-Bldg/Teaching-Assistant---MIMM-301---Scientific-Writing-Skills-in-MIMM--Winter-2027_JR0000080593": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant - MIMM 301 - Scientific Writing Skills in MIMM  Winter 2027",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Microbiology & Immunology Course Title: Scientific Writing Skills in MIMM Course Code: MIMM 301 Estimated Number of Positions: 2 Total Hours of Work per Term: 45 Position Summary: To answer student questions on the discussion board and via email To set up and correct quizzes To assist in the logistics of grading writing assignments To correct assignments To provide support to students writing their outline and paper Assist faculty members with scheduling meetings with students throughout the semester as well as answer any emails from students. Host and coordinate a journal club with students. Assist with entering grades into a spreadsheet. Qualifications: The position is open to graduate students at McGill University with a background in microbiology and immunology. Exceptional mastery of written English. Language Requirements (if relevant):    Effective communication skills in English are essential. An effective communication skill in French is desirable. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2027-01-05 Position End Date: 2027-04-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-01 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
