    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Duff-Medical-Bldg/Teaching-Assistant---Introductory-Immunology---MIMM-214---Winter-2027_JR0000080565": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant - Introductory Immunology - MIMM 214 - Winter 2027",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Microbiology & Immunology  Course Title: Introductory Immunology Course Code: MIMM 214 Estimated Number of Positions: 4 Total Hours of Work per Term: 100 Position Summary: Correct formative assessments. Organize pre-exam review sessions (2 sessions, one before the midterm and another one before the final). Answer emails and discussion board questions from students promptly. Answer questions from TEAM members. Provide support invigilating the quizzes and the midterm. Provide support and feedback to the professor in the preparation and logistics of teaching during the semester. Host quizzes and midterm viewing sessions.  Qualifications: The TA must be enrolled in a graduate Studies Program in Microbiology and Immunology or pursuing a graduate degree with a focus on immunology, work on a project with a focus on immunology, and/or with a strong track record as a previous student in MIMM214. A solid understanding of immunology is a must.   Language Requirements (if relevant):    Effective communication skills in English are essential. An effective communication skill in French is desirable. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based/located McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2027-01-05 Position End Date: 2027-04-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-24 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McIntyre--Medical/Job-Posting-Title-Teaching-Assistant---Principles-of-Toxicology---PHAR-303---Winter-2027_JR0000081161": {
      "title": "Job Posting Title Teaching Assistant - Principles of Toxicology - PHAR 303 - Winter 2027",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Pharmacology & Therapeutics Course Title: Principles of Toxicology Course Code: PHAR 303 Estimated Number of Positions: 2 Total Hours of Work per Term: 60 Position Summary: Coordinate and run tutorials. Coordinate and manage student PowerPoint and oral presentations. Setting up and invigilate exams. Provide individualized assistance to students having difficulty with the course material, including small group tutorial sessions. Grade exam short essays and posters. Answer questions on the myCourses platform.    Qualifications: Graduate student who has successfully passed PHAR 303 and PHAR 563 or equivalent. Must have sufficient command of English to be able to help international students.  Very good communication skills and attention to detail.    Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2027-01-05 Position End Date: 2027-04-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-01 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Sherbrooke-680/Communications-Assistant-A_JR0000081134": {
      "title": "Communications Assistant A",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Languages, Literatures, and Cultures The German Studies program, in collaboration with the Goethe-Institut Montréal, is organizing an exhibit on Gottfried Fuchs. The Department of Languages, Literatures, and Cultures a has the opportunity to host the exhibit for a two-week period in Fall 2026 and is seeking a Communications Assistant A for this exhibit. Position Summary: • Help produce promotional materials • Communicate with guests/partners on very speciﬁc tasks that the supervisor delegates them • Transport the posters to and from McGill • Help hang up and take down posters • Organize refreshments and other small things for the reception • Other light tasks Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities • Speak German (at least at an intermediate level) This position is covered by the AMUSE Collective Agreement. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level #4 on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma Minimal or No Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE A) $20.00 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 3 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-10-05 Position End Date: 2026-10-08 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-02 This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
