    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Duff-Medical-Bldg/Teaching-Assistant---MIMM-413--Parasitology-Winter-2027_JR0000080606": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant - MIMM 413- Parasitology Winter 2027",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Microbiology & Immunology Course Title: Parasitology Course Code: MIMM 413 Estimated Number of Positions: 5 Total Hours of Work per Term: 120 Position Summary: Meeting with the course coordinators and technicians once a week to discuss lab set up and protocols prior to each lab.  Help to set up labs before students arrive and put away equipment after the lab session. Supervise the students during weekly lab sessions including answering student questions about the lab, how to use lab equipment, work safely, calibrate equipment including microscopes, show students parasite specimens under the microscope. Show students how to interpret laboratory results. Correct lab reports and communicate with students by email or in person to answer questions. Help set up and correct lab exam at end of semester. Qualifications Required: Have general knowledge of Immunology & Microbiology and key research methods including PCR, ELISA Western blotting and use of light microscopes. Must have knowledge of parasitology and preferably have previously taken MIMM 413.  Language Requirements (if relevant):    Effective communication skills in English are essential. An effective communication skill in French is desirable. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2027-01-05 Position End Date: 2027-04-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-01 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McConnell-Eng-Bldg/Grader--ECSE-396---397---496---497--F26-_JR0000081220": {
      "title": "Grader -ECSE 396,  397,  496,  497 (F26)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Grader positions in the Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering for the Fall 2026 semester. These positions are open to McGill University students only. Hiring Unit: Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering Application Deadline: September 30, 2026 at 11:59 p.m. Effective Dates of Appointment: October 1 to December 21, 2026 *IMPORTANT: Candidates not currently employed by McGill must use a personal email when creating an account to submit their application. Do not use @mail.mcgill.ca or @mcgill.ca accounts for this. * Candidates currently employed by McGill must apply directly through the Career icon in their Workday profile.  Course Title and Course Number: Grader -ECSE 396, ECSE 397, ECSE 496, ECSE 497 (F26) ; Prof. Odile Liboiron-Ladouceur - 25 hours The grader is responsible for grading assigned assessments (Project Statements, Progress Reports, and Mid-Project reports), entering grades and applicable graduate-attribute assessments in myCourses, and providing feedback to students according to the rubrics and instructions provided by the courses instructors.   Salary: $17/h Hourly Salary: $17.00 Position Start Date: 2026-09-25 Position End Date: 2026-12-21 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-30 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
