    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Duff-Medical-Bldg/Teaching-Assistant--MIMM-385--Laboratory-in-Immunology-Winter-2027_JR0000080597": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant- MIMM 385- Laboratory in Immunology Winter 2027",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Microbiology & Immunology Course Title: Laboratory in Immunology Course Code: MIMM 385 Estimated Number of Positions: 8 Total Hours of Work per Term: 134 Position Summary: Grading short written answers in quizzes and exams according to an outlined format for the answers.  Entering these grades into a spreadsheet. Assist with the uploading of course content/managing student questions/comments on MyCourses. Instruct and guide 10-16 undergraduate students in a practical course on research techniques and theory in Immunology and grade them in various assessments such as participation, reports and presentations. Teaching assistants (TAs) are expected to read the week’s material and be prepared before the Wednesday afternoon lab sessions. They will attend TA meetings with the instructor on Friday afternoons, after the follow-up lab sessions. TAs will be present with their students in the Duff C-floor labs on Wednesday and Friday afternoons. TAs are responsible for instructing the students on safe laboratory procedures. In addition, TAs will respond to student questions through email and/or office hours. In the event of extraordinary circumstances beyond the University’s control, the content, schedule and/or evaluation scheme in this course is subject to change. In this case, TA duties would be adjusted accordingly. Qualifications Required: Preferably knowledge of Immunology & Microbiology and key research methods, and ideally having taken MIMM 211 and MIMM 214, MIMM 314 or MIMM 385. A solid understanding of immunology is a must.   Language Requirements (if relevant):    Effective communication skills in English are essential. An effective communication skill in French is desirable. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2027-01-05 Position End Date: 2027-04-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-01 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
