    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Macdonald-Eng-Bldg/Research-Assistant-2_JR0000081173": {
      "title": "Research Assistant 2",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-29\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary: We currently have an opening position as a Research Assistant 2 (RA2) working with Prof. Gaskin. Responsibilities: Literature review of numerical models of river confluence mixing.- Investigation of the parameters affecting the mixing layer in the depth averaged river model (TELEMAC) Field study to obtain velocity data in a profile across the mixing layer (ADV) Validation of numerical model/identification of modelling constraints Qualifications: Education/Experience: Masters of Engineering in Civil Engineering in the area of hydraulics or Integrated Water Resources Management with an internship project in hydraulics. B.Eng. in Civil Engineering. Knowledge of depth averaged modelling of river flows (TELEMAC), knowledge of GIS. Other Qualifying Skills and Abilities: Ability to use scientific instruments and machines Ability to apply critical thinking to laboratory procedures. Ability to observe, collect, and record data Ability to provide guidance and to work alongside other research assistants and established academic leaders Excellent communication, interpersonal and teamwork skills Knowledge of French and English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level #4  on a scale of 0-4. Posting expiry date: October 6, 2026 Supervisor: Prof. Gaskin Schedule: Part time, 18 hours, schedule to be determined with supervisor. Place: Gaskin Environmental Hydraulics Laboratory Pay: $32.15/hour Dates: October 7, 2026 - December 31, 2026 This position is covered by the Association of McGill University Research Employees (AMURE) collective agreement. Hourly Salary: $32.15 Hours per Week: 18 (Part time) Location: Macdonald Eng. Bldg. Supervisor: Professor Position Start Date: 2026-10-01 Position End Date: 2026-12-31 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-06 This position is covered by the Association of McGill University Research Employees (AMURE) collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Macdonald-Eng-Bldg/Course-Lecturer--Winter-2027--MECH-315---Intermediate-Dynamics_JR0000080833": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer (Winter 2027) MECH 315 – Intermediate Dynamics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-29\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Department of Mechanical Engineering Faculty of Engineering McGill University Winter 2027 Course Lecturer Position Deadline to Apply: October 14, 2026 The Department of Mechanical Engineering is inviting applications for a course lecturer position to teach in Winter 2027. Please include your cover letter and Curriculum Vitae. MECH 315 – Intermediate Dynamics (4 credits) Instructor must cover all material as written in the Course Outline on the McGill Course Catalogue page, as follows: Single-degree-of-freedom systems; free vibrations; effect of damping; response to harmonic, periodic and arbitrary excitation. Lagrange's equations of motion. Vibrations of multi-degree-of-freedom systems. Continuous systems. Teaching Qualification Requirements: Minimum of Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering. Minimum of three years’ experience teaching or in industry. Demonstrated knowledge of spoken and written English. Understanding cross-cultural practices. Strong problem-solving skills and flexible approach to teaching. Date: January 5, 2027 - April 30, 2027 Salary: $15,765 per course Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-14 For any questions, please contact apptadmin.mecheng@mcgill.ca. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hiring Unit: Department of Mechanical Engineering Course Title: Intermediate Dynamics Subject Code: MECH 315 Location: BURN 934 Schedule: Tuesday and Thursday 08:35 am-10:25 am Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-14 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Meredith-LadyHouse/Communications-Assistant-C_JR0000081282": {
      "title": "Communications Assistant C",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-29\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Faculty Development Office Position Summary: FacED needs help with the following tasks: Create online courses from the content created by the FacED team. Adapt older versions of FacED’s online offerings (e.g., teaching Journey, Peer Coaching). Troubleshooti any online course related difficulties with the FacED team. Develop and configure course structure in MyCourses, including building the initial structure, entering required course information, and importing instructional content created in Rise 360. Create and manage badges, awards, certificates of completion and intelligent agents on myCourses. Check that Course Merchant links work properly. Brainstorm solutions when there are difficulties in accessing a course. Compile completed Microsoft forms responses in online courses . This list is representative and not a complete and detailed list of tasks. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities Advanced knowledge of audio/video or graphic software is required. Skills needed: Video editing Building Online courses using content provided by our team Proficiency at learning and adopting new technologies (e.g., myCourses, Articulate, Camtesia) Bilingual French and Englis h Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # 4 (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma 2 Years Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE C) $29.00 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 10 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-10-13 Position End Date: 2027-04-12 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-06 This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
