    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Burnside-Hall/Course-Lecturer---MATH-266-001--W27-_JR0000081374": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer - MATH 266-001 (W27)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Course Information: Course Title and Number: MATH 266-001 Theory & Numerics of Ordinary & Partial Differential Equations Course Dates: January 5, 2027 to April 14, 2027 TEACHING QUALIFICATION REQUIREMENTS : Education : •             Ph.D. in Mathematical Sciences Experience : •             Expertise in content area of the course. •             Previous experience as an instructor at the university-level. •             Evidence of teaching excellence. Other: •             Excellent English and communication skills. A very strong mathematical background is required. Hiring Unit: Mathematics and Statistics Course Title: Theory & Numerics of Ordinary & Partial Differential Equations Subject Code: MATH 266 001 Location: MDHAR G-10 Schedule: TR 08:35 - 09:55 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-09 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
