      "title": "Course Lecturer – ECON 305-001 – Winter 2027",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Department of Economics Faculty of Arts McGill University Winter 2027 Course Lecturer Position Deadline to Apply: October 15, 2026 The Department of Economics is inviting applications for a course lecturer position to teach in Winter 2027. Please include your Cover Letter and Curriculum Vitae and if applicable a copy of your Study/Work Permit. A brief course outline is optional. ECON 305-001 Industrial Organization (3 Credits – CAP 90) The course analyzes the structure, conduct, and performance of industries, particularly but not exclusively in Canada. Topics include effects of mergers, barriers to entry, product line and promotion policies, vertical integration, and R & D policies of firms. Teaching Qualification Requirements: Doctoral level study in Economics, including completed comprehensive examinations for the PhD, or completed PhD degree in Economics; Evidence of highly effective teaching ability or of superior communications skills and potential for teaching excellence; The candidate's area of specialization should be as close as possible to that of the course being offered; Experience as a teaching assistant for a course is an asset. Friday 11:35 am-02:25 pm, January 5, 2027 – April 14, 2027. Location: RPHYS 118. Salary: $11,824 per course. For any questions, please contact Judy Dear , Area Manager, Human Resources & Operations. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the camp