    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Leacock-Building/Course-Lecturer---ECON-225-001---Winter-2027_JR0000081234": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer – ECON 225-001 – Winter 2027",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Department of Economics Faculty of Arts McGill University Winter 2027 Course Lecturer Position Deadline to Apply: October 15, 2026 The Department of Economics is inviting applications for a course lecturer position to teach in Winter 2027. Please include your Cover Letter and Curriculum Vitae and if applicable a copy of your Study/Work Permit. A brief course outline is optional. ECON 225-001 Economics of the Environment (3 Credits – CAP 321) A study of the application of economic theory to questions of environmental policy. Particular attention will be given to the measurement and regulation of pollution, congestion and waste and other environmental aspects of specific economies. Teaching Qualification Requirements: Doctoral level study in Economics, including completed comprehensive examinations for the PhD, or completed PhD degree in Economics; Evidence of highly effective teaching ability or of superior communications skills and potential for teaching excellence; The candidate's area of specialization should be as close as possible to that of the course being offered; Experience as a teaching assistant for a course is an asset. Monday and Wednesday 05:35 pm-06:55 pm, January 5, 2027 – April 14, 2027. Location: STBIO S1/4. Salary: $11,824 per course. For any questions, please contact Judy Dear , Area Manager, Human Resources & Operations. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hiring Unit: Department of Economics Course Title: Economics of the Environment Subject Code: ECON 225 001 Location: STBIO S1/4 Schedule: Monday and Wednesday 05:35 pm-06:55 pm Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-15 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McIntyre--Medical/Teaching-Assistant---Epigenetic-Drugs-and-Targets---PHAR-565---Winter-2027_JR0000081265": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant - Epigenetic Drugs and Targets - PHAR 565 - Winter 2027",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Pharmacology & Therapeutics Course Title: Epigenetic Drugs and Targets - PHAR 565 Course Code: PHAR 565 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 45 Position Summary: Tutoring, Invigilating exam.  Marking of exams and reviewing exams with students as needed. Monitoring and evaluating in-class presentations and discussions.  Help with management of myCourses website for the course. Qualifications: Graduate student who has successfully passed PHAR 562 and PHAR 563. Must have sufficient command of English to be able to help international students. Very good communication skills and attention to detail.  Knowledge of myCourses is an asset. Basic knowledge of epigenetics and epigenomics is also an asset.  Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2027-01-05 Position End Date: 2027-04-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-01 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
