    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McGill-College-2001/Faculty-Lecturer-General-Dentistry_JR0000080781": {
      "title": "Faculty Lecturer-General Dentistry",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\n​ Please refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position description The Faculty of Dental Medicine and Oral Health Sciences at McGill University is a dynamic faculty with a strong record of national and international leadership in the advancement of dental education, research and the profession. We are inviting applications for a part-time Ranked Contract Academic Staff Position at the level of Faculty Lecturer in the field of General Dentistry starting in the academic year 2026-2027. This is a ranked appointment as a member of the Contract Academic Staff and does not confer eligibility for tenure. The primary responsibility of the successful candidate will be clinical supervision and clinical teaching in the field of oral diagnosis, preventive dentistry & periodontics, oral radiology but can be extended to comprehensive care.  Community-oriented responsibilities will also be expected, commensurate with the importance the Faculty places on these areas. We seek to recruit well-rounded, enthusiastic individuals who champion Faculty vision, mission and shared values. Candidates must be committed to showing leadership in the areas of interest. Job Duties Successful applicants will be expected to: Provide clinical training/teaching to undergraduate students. Supervise students during clinical procedures while ensuring patient well-being and maintaining a supportive learning environment. Evaluate students and contribute to their professional development. Perform all professional dental duties in accordance with current standards of practice. Collaborate with faculty members and clinical training coordinators to ensure consistency in student supervision and the integration of evidence-based practice into professional care. Participate in all aspects of McGill’s academic mission (i.e. teaching and involvement in academic and administrative committees). Qualifications Applicants must have a D.M.D. or D.D.S. or equivalent from an accredited school. Applicants must be licensed or be eligible to be licensed by the Ordre des dentistes du Quebec. In accordance with career stage, candidates are expected to demonstrate evidence of recent clinical practice and high-quality teaching, inclusive pedagogy, and supervision of a diverse student body. Applicants who share our values and commitment to excellence in education, community service and research are encouraged to apply. Faculty/Department/Unit Faculty of Dental Medicine and Oral Health Sciences   Application deadline 30 October, 2026 Required Documents The following supporting documents are required: A cover letter The proof of DMD or DDS degree from a recognized accredited school curriculum vitae statement of teaching (for example, teaching statement, course materials) Provide evidence on teaching and educational skills and equivalent expertise in the field of interest. the names and contact information of three references from the previous institutions/organizations that they work in and a letter of the Dean of the Faculty that they have graduated from. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. McGill University is committed to equity and diversity within its community and values academic rigour and excellence. We welcome and encourage applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to engage productively with diverse communities. At McGill, research that reflects diverse intellectual traditions, methodologies, and modes of dissemination and translation is valued and encouraged. Candidates are invited to demonstrate their research impact both within and across academic disciplines and in other sectors, such as government, communities, or industry. McGill further recognizes and fairly considers the impact of leaves (e.g., family care or health-related) that may contribute to career interruptions or slowdowns. Candidates are encouraged to signal any leave that affected productivity, or that may have had an effect on their career path. This information will be considered to ensure the equitable assessment of the candidate’s record. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated equity groups to self-identify. It further seeks to ensure the equitable treatment and full inclusion of persons with disabilities by striving for the implementation of universal design principles transversally, across all facets of the University community, and through  accommodation policies and procedures . Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Macdonald-Eng-Bldg/Course-Lecturer--Winter-2027--MECH-546---Finite-Element-Methods-in-Solid-Mechanics_JR0000080943": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer (Winter 2027) MECH 546 - Finite Element Methods in Solid Mechanics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Department of Mechanical Engineering Faculty of Engineering McGill University   Winter 2027 Course Lecturer Position Deadline to Apply October 14, 2026 The Department of Mechanical Engineering is inviting applications for a course lecturer position to teach in Winter 2027. Please include your cover letter and Curriculum Vitae. Course Lecturer MECH 546 - Finite Element Methods in Solid Mechanics (3 credits) Instructor must cover all material as written in the Course Outline on the McGill Course Catalogue page, as follows: Discrete systems; variational formulation and approximation for continuous systems; direct and variational methods of element formulation in 1- 2- and 3 dimensions; formulation of isoparametric finite elements; plate and shell elements; finite element method for static analysis, vibration analysis and structural dynamics; introduction to nonlinear problems. Teaching Qualification Requirements: Minimum of Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering. Minimum of three years’ experience teaching or in industry. Demonstrated knowledge of spoken and written English. Understanding cross-cultural practices. Strong problem-solving skills and flexible approach to teaching. Date: January 5, 2027 - April 30, 2027 Salary: $11,824 per course Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-14 For any questions, please contact apptadmin.mecheng@mcgill.ca Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hiring Unit: Department of Mechanical Engineering Course Title: Finite Element Methods in Solid Mechanics Subject Code: MECH 546 Location: ENGTR 2110 Schedule: Tuesday and Thursday 2:35pm – 3:55 pm Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-14 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Macdonald-Eng-Bldg/Course-Lecturer--Winter-2027--MECH-539----Computational-Aerodynamics_JR0000080935": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer (Winter 2027) MECH 539 -  Computational Aerodynamics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Department of Mechanical Engineering Faculty of Engineering McGill University Winter 2027 Course Lecturer Position Deadline to Apply October 14, 2026 The Department of Mechanical Engineering is inviting applications for a course lecturer position to teach in Winter 2027. Please include your cover letter and Curriculum Vitae. Course Lecturer MECH 539-  Computational Aerodynamics (3 credits) Instructor must cover all material as written in the Course Outline on the McGill Course Catalogue page, as follows: Fundamental equations. Basic flow singularities. Boundary element methods. Source, doublet and vortex panel methods for 2D and 3D incompressible and compressible flows. Method of characteristics. Euler equations for inviscid rotational flows. Finite-difference and finite-volume methods. Explicit and implicit time-integration methods. Quasi 1D solutions. Nozzle and confined aerofoil applications. Teaching Qualification Requirements: Minimum of Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering and/or Electrical Engineering. Preference will be given to those with work and/or research experience focused on aircraft dynamics and control. Minimum of five years’ experience in the analysis and/or design of control systems. Prior experience in teaching.  Familiarity with state-space modeling, analysis of control stability and other advanced control topics. Demonstrated knowledge of spoken and written English. Strong problem-solving skills and flexible approach to teaching. Awareness of cross-cultural practices.  Date: January 5, 2027 - April 30, 2027 Salary: $11,824 per course Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-14   For any questions, please contact apptadmin.mecheng@mcgill.ca Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hiring Unit: Department of Mechanical Engineering Course Title: Computational Aerodynamics Subject Code: MECH 539 Location: ENGTR 0060 Schedule: Wednesday and Friday 11:35 am – 12:55 pm Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-14 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Macdonald-Eng-Bldg/Course-Lecturer--Winter-2027--MECH-532---Aircraft-Performance--Stability-and-Control_JR0000080928": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer (Winter 2027) MECH 532 - Aircraft Performance, Stability and Control",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Department of Mechanical Engineering Faculty of Engineering McGill University Winter 2027 Course Lecturer Position Deadline to Apply October 14, 2026 The Department of Mechanical Engineering is inviting applications for a course lecturer position to teach in Winter 2027. Please include your cover letter and Curriculum Vitae. Course Lecturer MECH 532 - Aircraft Performance, Stability and Control (3 credits) Instructor must cover all material as written in the Course Outline on the McGill Course Catalogue page, as follows: Aircraft performance criteria such as range, endurance, rate of climb, maximum ceiling for steady and accelerated flight. Landing and take-off distances. Static and dynamic stability in the longitudinal (stick-fixed and stick-free) and coupled lateral and directional modes. Control response for all three modes. Teaching Qualification Requirements: Minimum of Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering and/or Aerospace Engineering. Preference will be given to those with work and/or research experience focused on aircraft dynamics and control. Demonstrated knowledge of spoken and written English. Understanding cross-cultural practices. Strong problem-solving skills and flexible approach to teaching. Date: January 5, 2027 - April 30, 2027 Salary: $11,824 per course Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-14 For any questions, please contact apptadmin.mecheng@mcgill.ca Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hiring Unit: Department of Mechanical Engineering Course Title: Aircraft Performance, Stability and Control Subject Code: MECH 513 Location: ENGTR 0060 Schedule: Tuesday 5:35 pm - 8:25 pm Deadline to Apply: McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Macdonald-Eng-Bldg/Course-Lecturer--Winter-2027--MECH-513---Control-Systems_JR0000080835": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer (Winter 2027) MECH 513 – Control Systems",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Department of Mechanical Engineering Faculty of Engineering McGill University Winter 2027 Course Lecturer Position Deadline to Apply October 14, 2026 The Department of Mechanical Engineering is inviting applications for a course lecturer position to teach in Winter 2027. Please include your cover letter and Curriculum Vitae. MECH 513 – Control Systems (3 credits) Instructor must cover all material as written in the Course Outline on the McGill Course Catalogue page, as follows: State-space modelling and related linear algebra. Controllability and observability of linear time-invariant systems and corresponding tests, system realizations. Stability: Bounded-Input-Bounded-Output (BIBO), internal, Lyapunov. Linear state feedback control: pole placement and root locus design methods, linear quadratic regulator. State observers: full- and reduced-order designs, separation principle, Linear Quadratic Gaussian (LQG) design. Introduction to optimal control and optimal state estimation. Teaching Qualification Requirements: Minimum of Ph.D. degree in Mechanical or Electrical Engineering.  Minimum of five years’ experience in the analysis and/or design of control systems. Prior experience in teaching.  Familiarity with state-space modeling, analysis of control stability and other advanced control topics.  Demonstrated knowledge of spoken and written English.  Strong problem-solving skills and flexible approach to teaching.  Awareness of cross-cultural practices.  Date: January 5, 2027 - April 30, 2027 Salary: $11,824 per course Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-14 For any questions, please contact apptadmin.mecheng@mcgill.ca. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hiring Unit: Department of Mechanical Engineering Course Title: Control Systems Subject Code: MECH 513 Location: ENGTR 0060 Schedule: Tuesday 5:35 pm - 8:25 pm Deadline to Apply: McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Macdonald-Eng-Bldg/Course-Lecturer---Winter-2027----MECH-346-Heat-Transfer_JR0000080834": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer  (Winter 2027) - MECH 346 Heat Transfer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Department of Mechanical Engineering Faculty of Engineering McGill University Winter 2027 Course Lecturer Position Deadline to Apply October 14, 2026 at 11:59 p.m. The Department of Mechanical Engineering is inviting applications for a course lecturer position to teach in Winter 2027. Please include your cover letter and Curriculum Vitae. Course Lecturer MECH 346 Heat Transfer Instructor must cover all material as written in the Course Outline on the McGill Course Catalogue page, as follows: Basic concepts and overview. Steady and unsteady heat conduction. Fin Theory. Convective heat transfer: governing equations; dimensionless parameters; analogy between momentum and heat transfer. Design correlations for forced, natural, and mixed convection. Heat exchangers. Radiative heat transfer: black- and gray-body radiation; shape factors; enclosure theory. Thermal engineering design project. Teaching Qualification Requirements: Minimum of a Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering. Evidence of highly effective teaching ability or of superior communications skills and potential for teaching excellence with previous teaching experience. Strong problem-solving skills. The candidate area of specialization should be as close as possible to that of the course being offered. Demonstrated knowledge of spoken and written English. Understanding cross-cultural practices. Date: January 5, 2027 – April 30, 2027 Salary: $11,824 per course Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-14 For any questions, please contact apptadmin.mecheng@mcgill.ca Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hiring Unit: Department of Mechanical Engineering Course Title: Heat Transfer Subject Code: MECH 346 Location: ENGMC 13 Schedule: Wednesday and Friday 2:35 pm – 3:55pm Deadline to Apply: McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
