    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Raymond-Building/Course-Lecturer---NUTR-343_JR0000081116": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer - NUTR 343",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). School of Human Nutrition Faculty of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences Winter 2027 Course Lecturer Position Deadline to Apply: October 15, 2026 Teaching Qualification Requirements: Teaching responsibility and cost control related to the nutrition and food service environment. OTHER: Use of financial statement and systems for decision making. EDUCATION: Master’s in business, management or related discipline Schedule: Thursdays 2:35 pm-5:25 pm Location: Raymond Building, Room 4-045 Macdonald Campus Note: The McGill exam sessions take place over two weeks after the end of classes, and Course Lecturers are expected to be available on the day of a scheduled final exam and are required to grade final exams as part of their contract . Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hiring Unit: School of Human Nutrition Course Title: Financial Management and Accounting Subject Code: NUTR 343 Location: Raymond 4-045 Schedule: Thursdays 2:35pm-5:25pm Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-15 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
