    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Montreal-Neuro/Clinical-Research-Coordinator_JR0000081453": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-30\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary: Administer, analyze, supervise, manage, or direct the activities related to enhancing and promoting the University’s research, innovation, and collaboration activities, thereby furthering its reputation as a leading research university in Canada. Deliver comprehensive services and strategies related to sponsored research, innovation, partnerships, and ethics review and compliance. Identify research funding opportunities, support the development of funding applications, as well as nominations for prizes and awards, promote development and invention, and create and strengthen internal and external collaborations. Primary Responsibilities: Administer clinical trial screening activities across multiple sites (e.g. ophthalmology clinic, radiology clinic, assessments at the Glen site, etc.) to ensure timely patient enrollment and alignment with project goals. Oversee recruitment efforts by serving as first point of contact for recruitment activities, including identifying eligible participants, performing chart reviews, and completing the informed consent process in collaboration with treating teams. Support study pre-activation activities and all ongoing activities by coordinating logistics such as vendor scheduling, calendar building, monitor visits, and preparation of regulatory and study binders. Collect and transcribe clinical and cognitive outcome assessments, patient-reported outcomes, and laboratory data; enter and verify data in sponsor platforms in accordance with regulatory guidelines. Submit and maintain ethics applications, amendments, and renewals in  our research platform, ensuring compliance with REB, institutional, and sponsor requirements. Liaise with physicians, nurses, laboratory staff, vendors, and sponsors to communicate study-related updates, patient eligibility, and protocol changes in a timely manner. Participate in internal and external meetings and act as liaison between the sponsor, research team, and participants. Track and report recruitment metrics and ensure documentation of protocol deviations, adverse events, and investigator oversight is complete and up to date. Facilitate knowledge transfer when work needs to be redistributed across the team. - Assist with supply shipment coordination, and other administrative tasks based on specific needs directly related to the studies Perform study specific assessments and the related training, including proper setup, administration, and documentation as required and determined by the study protocol. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities Undergraduate Degree (Biology or Sciences). Fluent in French and English required. Two years clinical research experience required. Previous experience with patients required. Proven organizational skills. Must be able to manage multiple activities and projects simultaneously. Ability to troubleshoot, solve problems, take initiative, and prioritize work. At ease with technology and troubleshooting tech-related problems. Experience with elderly, mobility-reduced, and other vulnerable patient populations an asset. Flexibility to work in different disease areas required, as operationally needed. As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level 4 on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: DEC III 3 Years Related Experience / Hourly Salary: (MUNACA Level H) $33.05 - $40.97 Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Research Advisor Position End Date (If applicable): 2027-10-18 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-14 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McIntyre--Medical/Teaching-Assistant---PHGY-560---Light-Microscopy-for-the-Life-Science---Winter-2027_JR0000081579": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant - PHGY 560 - Light Microscopy for the Life Science - Winter 2027",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-30\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department Of Physiology Course Title: Light Microscopy for the Life Science Course Code: PHGY 560 Estimated Number of Positions: 2 Total Hours of Work per Term: 45 Position Summary: Attend 6 lab sessions of 2 hours Attend 6 pre-lab meetings, review labs, laboratory preparation Assist instructor in marking student lab reports Assist instructor in marking student tests Qualifications: B.Sc. in Science Familiar with microscopes, digital imaging and image         processing and analysis.  Previous students from PHGH 560 would be ideal. Ability to assess written work and clearly express written criticisms. Effective communication skills in English are essential. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2027-01-05 Position End Date: 2027-04-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-01 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/Student-Research-Assistant_JR0000081082": {
      "title": "Student Research Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-30\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Job Description: Dr. Zanazanian is an interdisciplinary researcher whose work explores historical consciousness and the ways in which people construct, interpret, and use historical knowledge to make sense of the world around them. The project brings together four different practitioner areas, with four co-principal investigators contributing perspectives from different disciplines. We are currently seeking four Research Assistants, with one RA connected to each of the following areas: Gastroenterology / Emergency Room Medicine, Clinical Psychology, Community Development, Performing Arts. He is looking to recruit 4 research assistants (RA) to work on a large-scale interdisciplinary research project. The anticipated responsibilities are subject to change but would broadly be: Conducting literature reviews related to your assigned disciplinary area Identifying and organizing relevant academic literature Reviewing and editing literature reviews Helping synthesize research across disciplines Participating in research meetings and discussions Attending library and research-methods workshops Contributing to the development of interdisciplinary research materials Please note that 1 in-person meeting of 2-3 hours is required weekly . Currently the suggested time is Fridays from 3-4pm. This is a particularly interesting opportunity for students who want experience with largescale, interdisciplinary research and who are interested in seeing how knowledge is constructed differently across professional and academic fields. All students are welcome to apply (keep in mind the targeted disciplines ). You do not need to be studying Education or History. We are specifically looking for students whose academic, professional, or research experiences connect them to one of the four practitioner areas: Gastroenterology / Emergency Room Medicine, Clinical Psychology, Community Development, Performing Arts. In your cover letter, please clearly indicate: 1. Which of the four fields you are connected to 2. How you are connected to that field (for example, through your program of study, professional experience, research, clinical experience, community involvement, or another relevant connection) 3. Why you are interested in participating in an interdisciplinary research project 4. Any relevant experience you have with research, literature reviews, academic writing, or working across disciplines Qualifications Required (skills and abilities, language skills): Connection to one of the four practitioner areas (Gastroenterology / Emergency Room Medicine, Clinical Psychology, Community Development, Performing Arts). Strong English language skills as the position requires frequent writing tasks. Education/experience requirement : Graduate student Additional qualifying skills and abilities : Experience with academic research, research writing, literature reviews Appointment dates: September 30, 2026 - December 15, 2026 Hourly Rate : $22.00/hour Schedule/Hours per week : 5 hours/week (part-time) Immediate Supervisor : Prof. Paul Zanazanian This position is covered by the Association of McGill University Research Employees (AMURE) collective agreement. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $22.00 Hours per Week: 5 (Part time) Location: Education Building Supervisor: Associate Professor Position Start Date: 2026-09-30 Position End Date: 2026-12-15 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-04 This position is covered by the Association of McGill University Research Employees (AMURE) collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McIntyre--Medical/Teaching-Assistant---PHGY-351---Research-Techniques-in-Physiology---Winter-2027_JR0000081560": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant - PHGY 351 - Research Techniques in Physiology - Winter 2027",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-30\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Physiology Course Title: Research Techniques in Physiology Course Code: PHGY 351 Estimated Number of Positions: 4 Total Hours of Work per Term: 20 Position Summary: Help run the weekly quizzes and marking.  Lab related Work : Prepare the experiments  and demonstrate critical steps for the labor experiments listed below: Tissue culture cells growing and propagation site directed mutagenesis -PCR-, Bacterial transformation, Minipreps Restriction digestion and analysis, DNA sequencing analysis ​Transient transfection and mounting slides for confocal microscopy Help to prepare the flow cytometry datasets needed for the data analysis sessions. Share the flow cytometry datasets with the students, ensuring all students managed to download the data ahead of the class. Advise students in advance of the class how to download the free trial version of FlowJo software, troubleshooting any technical issues. Attend the lab sessions, monitor the chat section of the Zoom meeting to answer questions and troubleshoot problems. Grade lab reports Qualifications: B.Sc. in Science Registered graduate student at McGill University Experience in protein trafficking, cell culture and microscopy Effective communication skills in English are essential. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2027-01-05 Position End Date: 2027-04-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-01 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Day-ChancellorHall/Research-Assistant-Assistant-de-recherche---VMF-SSHRC260_JR0000081543": {
      "title": "Research Assistant/Assistant de recherche - VMF SSHRC260",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-30\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Job description : Assisting the professor with research and related duties in a project on faculty governance and fiduciary duties of university administrators. Duties will include preparation of critical bibliographies and literature reviews, case briefs, statutory review, citation checking, copy-editing, photocopying, and mailing   Qualifications : JD/BCL candidate in Year 2 or above; Ideally, should be taking or have taken Business Associations or a related course; Good organizational skills and copy-editorial knowledge; Prior coursework in or knowledge of political or legal theory and philosophy, theology or religious studies, and/or history is desirable. Other languages (especially French, German, Latin, Spanish, Italian) also valuable   Documents requested : CV, unofficial transcript, list or prior courses in related fields, one or two faculty references (may be from Law, undergrad, or Cégep).       Description of research project available here .   Hourly rate: $23.00 or more depending on qualifications and experience Weekly hours: 10-15 ___________________________________________   Description du poste : Assister le professeur dans ses travaux de recherche et les tâches connexes dans le cadre d’un projet portant sur la gouvernance universitaire et les obligations fiduciaires des administrateurs universitaires. Les tâches comprendront la préparation de bibliographies critiques et d’analyses documentaires, la rédaction de résumés de jurisprudence, l’examen des textes législatifs, la vérification des citations, la relecture, la photocopie et l’envoi postal.   Profil recherché : Étudiant en droit (JD/BCL) en deuxième année ou au-delà ; idéalement, en train de suivre ou ayant suivi le cours « Business Associations » ou un cours connexe ; bonnes compétences organisationnelles et connaissances en révision de textes ; des cours suivis ou des connaissances en théorie et philosophie politiques ou juridiques, en théologie ou en sciences religieuses, et/ou en histoire sont souhaitables. La maîtrise d’autres langues (notamment le français, l’allemand, le latin, l’espagnol et l’italien) constitue également un atout.     Documents requis : CV, relevé de notes non officiel, liste des cours suivis dans des domaines connexes, une ou deux lettres de recommandation de professeurs (issus de la faculté de droit, du premier cycle ou du cégep).   Description of research project available here .   Taux horaire : 23,00 $ ou plus, selon les qualifications et l’expérience.   Heures hebdomadaires : 10 à 15 Hourly Salary: $23.00 Hours per Week: 10 (Part time) Location: Day, Chancellor,Hall Supervisor: Associate Professor Position Start Date: 2026-10-19 Position End Date: 2027-06-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-07 This position is covered by the Association of McGill University Research Employees (AMURE) collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Centennial-Centre/Invigilator_JR0000081563": {
      "title": "Invigilator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-30\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). PLEASE NOTE : This position is required for the exam period taking place at MACDONALD CAMPUS . As part of application in Workday, please upload a summary of past experience as invigilators at McGill, as well as your AVAILABILITY during the Exam period dates mentioned below. Hiring Unit: Faculty of Agricultural & Environmental Sciences - MACDONALD CAMPUS Exam Period:   December 4 – December 22, 2026 Position Summary: Prepare the examination room prior to each session to specific requirements as well as ensuring that equipment and facilities are functioning properly. Assist professors with the distribution of their exams. Ensure that only students with valid identification enter the examination room. Monitor student activity to ensure exam integrity is maintained. Assists professors in obtaining student signatures on sign-in sheets. Escort students to the lavatory. Ensure that when the exam has officially ended students stop writing. Assist professors with the collection of exams. Ensure the examination room is cleaned and empty after examination. Other related duties as assigned.   Qualifications: Previous invigilating experience, an asset. Graduate Student preferred at McGill. Punctuality - work shift starts 30 minutes prior to scheduled start time of exams. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: (TSUM Invigilator) $18.00 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-13 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
