    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/Course-Lecturer-EDEC-301-001-DISE-W27_JR0000081174": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer EDEC 301-001 DISE W27",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course code and title: EDEC 301-001. Special Topics 2. Topic: Happiness in Education Description: Selected topics and contemporary developments in the areas of elementary and/or secondary education. The content will vary from year to year and will be announced prior to registration. This course is not Team taught or offered online. Term: Winter 2027 Credits: 3 credits Location: Education Building (EDUC 216) Schedule: Monday & Wednesday, 10:05 am-11:25 am Appointment dates: December 21, 2026 - April 30, 2027 Teaching Qualification Requirements (TQRs): Education: 1. Graduate degree in Education or a related field. PhD preferred. 2. Academic and/or professional background relevant to the announced special topic (see Other information). Experience: 1. Experience teaching and/or facilitating learning in educational or related professional contexts. 2. Experience designing and facilitating engaging, discussion-based, experiential, and/or inquiry-oriented learning. 3. Experience supporting learners in connecting educational concepts and scholarship to personal, professional, and/or educational contexts. Other: 1. Knowledge of the impact and experience integrating pedagogical approaches anchored to equity, diversity and inclusion 2. Familiarity using myCourses, Zoom and/or other similar online platforms to facilitate quality teaching and learning experiences 3. Familiarity with the application of a variety of digital teaching and learning tools 4. Familiarity teaching blended classes 5. Instruction in this course may be delivered remotely if indicated as required by the university. Other informatio n: Qualifications related to the special topic, Happiness in Education: 1.Teaching, research, and/or professional experience related to happiness, well-being, positive psychology, human flourishing, or related areas. 2.Demonstrated knowledge of: Research and theoretical perspectives related to happiness, well-being, positive psychology, and human flourishing, or related areas. Applications of research on happiness and well-being to educational contexts. Relationships among individual well-being, social relationships, empathy, meaning, and learning. Research-informed approaches and practices that support well-being and positive development. Experience facilitating experiential learning and reflective activities related to personal and/or professional development. Experience translating research and theory related to happiness and well-being into accessible and applied learning experiences. Posting Period: October 1 - October 15, 2026 (11:59 PM) Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located.   McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing.   Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course Title: Special Topics 2 Subject Code: EDEC 301 001 Location: Education Building Schedule: Monday & Wednesday 10:05 am-11:25 am Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-15 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/Course-Lecturer-EDEC-262-002-003-DISE-W27_JR0000081172": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer EDEC 262-002/003 DISE W27",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course code and title: EDEC 262-002/003. Media, Technology and Education. Description: Orientation to the equipment and systems of educational technology. Examination of theories of educational technology, media education and technology education and the exploration and development of possible applications in school settings. This course is not Team taught or offered online. Term: Winter 2027 Credits: 3 credits Location: Education Building (EDUC 129) Schedule: Thursday, 02:35 pm-05:25 pm Appointment dates: December 21, 2026 - April 30 , 2027 Teaching Qualification Requirements (TQRs): Education 1.MA in a relevant field (i.e. Critical  pedagogy  involving digital technologies  in education;  technology and media literacy applications in education). 2.PhD or equivalent in a relevant field is an asset. Experience 1.Demonstrated knowledge and experience in:  Pedagogical role of contemporary technological media in education across disciplines  Critical media literacy approaches  Foundational understanding of media education and its core tenets  Basic technology platforms and media production skills  How new media can be used in innovative ways to enhance learning  2.Experience with digital technology as a teacher/instructor or other education professional in the Quebec educational system. 3.Familiarity with the professional competencies specified by the Ministère de l’Éducation  Other 1.Previous successful experience teaching similar course(s) at the undergraduate or graduate level. 2.Knowledge of the impact and proven record integrating pedagogical approaches anchored to equity, diversity and inclusion.  3.Familiarity using myCourses, ZOOM and other similar online platforms to facilitate quality teaching and learning experiences.   4.Familiarity teaching blended classes is an asset.   5.Familiarity with the application of a variety of digital teaching and learning tools.  Other information: 1.Commitment to working with a team of committed and engaged instructors.  2.Must be available to attend course coordination and planning meeting minimum of 2 weeks in advance of course start date. Posting dates: October 1 - October 15, 2026 Deadline to apply : October 15 (11:59 PM) Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course Title: Media, Technology and Education Subject Code: EDEC 262 002/003 Location: Education Building Schedule: Thursday 02:35 pm-05:25 pm Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-15 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/Course-Lecturer-EDEC-249-003-004-DISE-W27_JR0000081167": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer EDEC 249-003/004 DISE W27",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course Code and Title: EDEC 249-003/004. Global Education & Social Justice. Description : A cross-curricular, interdisciplinary approach to teaching/creating learning experiences for students. It will foster critical thinking and nurture lifelong global understanding, active engagement and participation in relation to questions of social, economic, and environmental justice, by infusing these issues in the classroom. This course is not Team Taught or offered online. Term: Winter 2027 Course Credits : 3 Location: Education Building (EDUC 216) Schedule: Tuesday & Thursday, 02:35 pm-03:55 pm Appointment Dates: December 20, 2026 - April 30, 2027 Teaching Qualification Requirements (TQRs): Education: Master educator with an MA in a relevant field (i.e., curriculum studies, educational foundations - philosophy, sociology, and history of education, critical pedagogy, comparative education) and relevant professional experience as a school educator, pedagogue, community educator, and/or NGO organizer or educator. PhD or equivalent in a relevant field is an asset. Experience: 1. Demonstrated knowledge of: Global education issues Social justice issues in education Foundational issues in education Contemporary issues in education Comparative education 2. Previous experience teaching similar course(s) at the undergraduate or graduate level and/or equivalent relevant teaching or professional experience. 3. Experience as a school administrator, institutional leader, community leader, NGO organizer or educator, and/or teacher/instructor or other education professional in the Quebec educational system is an asset. Other: 1.Knowledge of the impact and proven record integrating pedagogical approaches anchored to equity, diversity and inclusion 2.Familiarity using myCourses, ZOOM and other similar online platforms to facilitate quality teaching and learning experiences 3.Familiarity teaching blended classes is an asset 4.Familiarity with the application of a variety of digital teaching and learning tools Posting Period: October 1-15, 2026 Deadline to apply : October 15 (11:59 PM) Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course Title: Global Education and Social Justice Subject Code: EDEC 249 003/004 Location: Education Building Schedule: Tuesday & Thursday 02:35 pm-03:55 pm Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-15 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityr