    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/Course-Lecturer-EDEC-221-003-004-DISE-W27_JR0000081149": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer EDEC 221-003/004 DISE W27",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course Description: EDEC 221-003/004. Leadership and Group Skills. Description : Management, effective team leadership, group dynamics, and communications skills crucial for leaders. Discussion of mainstream intercultural, Indigenous, international and institutional practices and leadership skills. This course is not Team Taught or offered online. Term: Winter 2027 Course Credits : 3 Location: Education Building (EDUC 216) Schedule: Wednesday & Friday, 02:35 pm-03:55 pm Appointment Dates: December 21, 2026 - April 30, 2027 Teaching Qualification Requirements (TQRs): Education: Master educator with a graduate degree in a relevant field (e.g. educational leadership, leadership studies, educational studies, organizational behaviour, management, social movements, group dynamics). PhD or equivalent in a relevant field is an asset (In exceptional circumstances applicants without a Master's degree but with significant research or professional experience related to the course content may be considered). Experience: Demonstrated knowledge of: A wide range of diverse leadership theories and approaches; Theories and philosophies about adult learning and group dynamics; Analysis and application of organizational factors (culture, structure, change, and development) on leadership practice and group behaviour Effective interpersonal communication techniques, including active listening, feedback, non-verbal communication, conflict resolution, and negotiation strategies. adult learning theories and team dynamics theories Practical experience working with diverse groups, including in intercultural or Indigenous contexts, and integrating diversity, equity, and inclusion principles into leadership practices. Experience facilitating group discussions and resolving interpersonal conflicts within teams Minimum of 5 years' experience in leadership roles within non-school, educational environments such as non-profits, government agencies, and/or private sector organizations. Demonstrated success teaching similar/related course(s) to adult learners in traditional or non-traditional educational settings and/or equivalent relevant teaching or professional experience. Other: Proven record implementing equity, diversity, and inclusion-centered pedagogical strategies; responsiveness to student needs and interests. Collaborative, with a commitment to working with a team of committed and engaged instructors. Familiarity with Learning Management Systems and other online tools to facilitate quality teaching and learning experiences. Must be available to attend course coordination and planning meetings in advance of course start date. Posting Period: October 1-15, 2026 Deadline to apply : October 15 (11:59 PM) Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course Title: Leadership and Group Skills Subject Code: EDEC 221 003/004 Location: Education Building Schedule: Wednesday & Friday 02:35 pm-03:55 pm Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-15 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/Course-Lecturer-EDEC-203-002-DISE-W27_JR0000081144": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer EDEC 203-002 DISE W27",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course code and title: EDEC 203-002. Communication in Education. (PIF) Description: Written and oral communication in Education: emphasis on strategies for identifying, analyzing and solving writing and speaking problems. Course work based on academic and professional communication in education, with a particular focus on classroom communication. This course is not Team taught or offered online. This course is taught in French. A high level of proficiency in French and ability to teach in French are required. Term: Winter 2027 Credits: 3 credits Location: Education Building (EDUC 613) Schedule: Wednesday, 02:35 pm-05:25 pm Appointment dates: December 21, 2026 - April 30, 2027 Teaching Qualification Requirements (TQRs): Education: 1. Master’s degree  (in exceptional circumstances applicants without a Master’s degree but with significant research or professional experience related to the course content may be considered). Experience: 1, Demonstrated knowledge of course content. 2. Knowledge of the Quebec Education program (QEP). 3. Familiarity with the Professional Competencies specified by the Ministere de l’Éducation. 4. Previous successful experience teaching similar course(s) to pre-service teachers an asset. 5. Experience teaching in the Quebec school system. Other: 1. Commitment to working with a team of committed and engaged instructors 2. Must be available to attend course coordination and planning meeting minimum of 2 weeks in advance of course start date. Additional Information: 1. Familiarity using MyCourses or similar online platforms. 2. Familiarity with online platforms such as ZOOM are an asset. 3. Familiarity with teaching blended classes. 4. Understandings about equity and diversity issues and how to address these in classrooms. 5. Technology skills to practice. Posting Period: October 1 - October 15 (11:59 PM) Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located.   McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing.   Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course Title: Communication in Education Subject Code: EDEC 203 002 Location: Education Building Schedule: Wednesday 02:35 pm-05:25 pm Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-15 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
