    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/Course-Lecturer-EDEM-646-025-DISE-W27_JR0000081278": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer EDEM 646-025 DISE W27",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course code and title: EDEM 646-025. Planning and Evaluation. Description: Focuses on contemporary approaches to planning, monitoring and evaluating programs across a range of contexts (K-graduation, college, non-governmental organization, adult education centre). Areas of study include adaptive and strategic management, results-based management, log frame analysis, systems assessment, stakeholder analysis, and fourth generation evaluation. This course is not Team taught. This course is offered online synchronously. Term: Winter 2027 Course Credits : 3 Location: Online (synchronous) Schedule: Tuesday, 05:35 pm-08:25 pm Appointment dates: December 21, 2026 - April 30, 2026 Teaching Qualification Requirements (TQRs): Education: 1.Master educator with an MA in a relevant field (curriculum studies, educational leadership or school administration) and/or extensive relevant experience as a school leader or pedagogue 2. PhD or equivalent in a relevant field is an asset ​Experience: 1.Expert knowledge of: Wide range of different theories and approaches to curriculum design, development, and implementation Theory and practice of educational leadership in Quebec and Canadian contexts Educational leadership in contemporary educational settings including but not limited to elementary and high schools and alternative schools 2.Experience as a school administrator, institutional leader, community leader and/or master teacher/instructor in the Quebec educational system Other: Previous successful experience teaching similar course(s) at the graduate level  Knowledge of the impact and proven record integrating pedagogical approaches anchored to equity, diversity and inclusion  Familiarity using myCourses, ZOOM and other similar online platforms to facilitate quality teaching and learning experiences   Familiarity teaching blended classes is an asset   Familiarity with the application of a variety of digital teaching and learning tools  Posting Period: October 1-15, 2026 Deadline to apply : October 15 (11:59 PM) Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course Title: Planning and Evaluation Subject Code: EDEM 646 025 Location: Online (synchronous) Schedule: Tuesday 05:35 pm-08:25 pm Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-15 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Life-Sciences-Bldg-/Research-Associate_JR0000081673": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). The Department of Microbiology and Immunology is seeking a highly motivated and accomplished full-time Research Associate to contribute to and advance research activities in the field of Microbiology and Immunology. Position Summary Reporting to the Principal Investigator, the successful candidate will develop and conduct research projects, provide scientific leadership and supervision within the research team, and support the achievement of the laboratory's research objectives. The incumbent will be responsible for the key responsibilities outlined below.   Key Responsibilities: Work in collaboration with the Research Supervisor to develop and conduct research projects and is responsible for achieving the project’s objectives. As required, the Research Associate is responsible for the functional supervision of the Research Assistant(s) and/or Undergraduate/Graduate Research Assistant. Develop and conduct research projects and protocols, processes and procedures as delegated by the Research Supervisor. Establish the design and development of research methods, data collection and analysis, and the interpretation of results. Write theoretical or methodological reports, papers or articles related to research activities. Assist with the preparation of grant applications. Organize, distribute and verify the work of research staff and participate in their training, including Research Assistants and Undergraduate/Graduate Student Research Assistants. Perform various administrative tasks related to research projects, including documentation, record maintenance, coordination of project activities, and preparation of research-related materials.   Qualifications and Experience:   Education: PhD in Microbiology and Immunology. Minimum of five (5) years of relevant postdoctoral research experience in Microbiology and Immunology or a closely related field. Experience and Skills: Experience with Animal infection models, flow cytometry, ELISA, animal colony management. Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a research environment. Experience supervising and mentoring research personnel and trainees. Language requirement: Knowledge of French and English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level #4  (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4. This position is covered by the Association of McGill University Research Employees (AMURE) collective agreement. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $35.37 Hours per Week: 35 (Full time) Location: Life Sciences Bldg . Supervisor: Professor Position Start Date: 2026-11-01 Position End Date: 2027-10-31 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-08 This position is covered by the Association of McGill University Research Employees (AMURE) collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/Course-Lecturer-EDEM-637-001-DISE-W27_JR0000081273-1": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer EDEM 637-001 DISE W27",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course code and title: EDEM 637-001. Managing Educational Change. Description : Explores conceptual approaches to managing school improvement and organizational change with applications such as conflict management, action planning, coaching, shared vision- building and problem solving. Uses relevant case studies to bring theory into practice. This course is not Team Taught or offered online. Term: Winter 2027 Course Credits: 3 Course Schedule: Wednesday, 05:35 pm-08:25 pm Location : SH680 1085 Appointment dates: December 21, 2026 - April 30, 2027 Teaching Qualification Requirements (TQRs): Education: 1.Master educator with an MA in a relevant field (i.e.. educational leadership or school administration) and/or extensive relevant experience as a school leader. 2.PhD or equivalent in a relevant field is an asset. Experience: 1. Expert knowledge of: Managing educational change particularly in the Quebec context. 2. Experience as a school administrator, institutional leader in the Quebec educational system. ​ Other: 1.Previous successful experience teaching similar course(s) at the graduate level. 2.Knowledge of the impact and proven record of integrating pedagogical approaches anchored to equity, diversity and inclusion. 3.Familiarity using myCourses, ZOOM and other similar online platforms to facilitate quality teaching and learning experiences. 4.Familiarity teaching blended classes is an asset. 5.Familiarity with the application of a variety of digital teaching and learning tools. Other information: ​ Requirements include: 1.A commitment of working with a team of committed and engaged instructors. 2.Must be available to attend course coordination and planning meeting minimum of 2 weeks in advance of course start date. Posting period: October 1 - October 15, 2026 Deadline to apply : October 15 (11:59 PM) Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing . Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course Title: Managing Educational Change Subject Code: EDEM 637 001 Location: SH680 1085 Schedule: Wednesday 05:35 pm-08:25 pm Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-15 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
