      "title": "Course Lecturer (EPIB 675) - Department of Epidemiology, Biostatistics & Occupational Health - Winter 2027",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Course Lecturer (EPIB 675) Winter 2027 EPIB 675 Spatial and Spatio-temporal epidemiology (3 credits) Winter 2027   Spatial and Spatio-temporal epidemiology : Study, through lectures, guided reading, practicals, assignments etc., of an elected and approved topic of epidemiologic importance.   Location: MC2001, 1203 Schedule:  Tuesday/Thursday, 1:05 to 2:25 Credits: 3   Teaching Qualification Requirements: Education:   MSc (or higher) in Biostatistics or Statistics Experience: Prior teaching experience in Biostatistics or Statistics. Prior teaching experience in Biostatistics or Statistics. Experience in Bayesian inference; Geostatistics, Disease mapping and computational languages such as Stan and Nimble. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. This posting will expire at 00:00 am the day of the deadline to apply. You have until midnight the day before the deadline to apply to submit your application. Hiring Unit: Department of Epidemiology, Biostatistics & Occupational Health Course Title: Spatial and Spatio-temporal epidemiology Subject Code: EPIB 675 Location: MC2001, 1203 Schedule: Tuesday/Thursday, 1:05 to 2:25 Deadline to Apply: 2