    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/Course-Lecturer-EDER-639-001-DISE-W27_JR0000081353": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer EDER 639-001 DISE W27",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course code and title: EDER 639-001. Education and Development. Description: Theories of development and the contribution of education to political, economic and social change. This course is not Team Taught or offered online. Term: Winter 2027 Course Credits : 3 Location: Education Building (EDUC 629) Schedule: Monday, 05:35 pm-08:25 pm  Appointment dates : December 21, 2026 - April 30, 2027 Teaching Qualification Requirements (TQRs): Education: 1.PhD in relevant fields (e.g., international development, education, sociology, or related interdisciplinary fields). Exceptionally, a completed master’s degree with extensive relevant experience may be considered. 2.Strong grounding in theories of development and their intersections with education in global contexts. Experience: 1.Demonstrated knowledge of: Major theories and paradigms in development, including modernization, dependency, postcolonial, decolonial, and alternative development approaches. The historical and ongoing relationships between education and development, including colonial and postcolonial dynamics. Global and local education issues in development contexts, including inequality, access, policy, and systems change. The role of education in addressing social, economic, and political challenges Contemporary issues in global development and their implications for education. 2.Experience teaching or facilitating learning in international, comparative, or development-focused education contexts. 3.Experience engaging students in critical analysis of theory and application to real-world cases. Other: 1.Knowledge of the impact and experience integrating pedagogical approaches anchored to equity, diversity and inclusion 2.Familiarity using myCourses, Zoom and/or other similar online platforms to facilitate quality teaching and learning experiences 3.Familiarity with the application of a variety of digital teaching and learning tools 4.Familiarity teaching blended classes 5.Instruction in this course may be delivered remotely if indicated as required by the university. Posting Period: October 1-15, 2026 Deadline to apply : October 15 (11:59 PM) Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course Title: Education and Development. Subject Code: EDER 639 001 Location: Education Building Schedule: Monday 05:35 pm-08:25 pm Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-15 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/Course-Lecturer-EDES-353-001-002-DISE-W27_JR0000081392": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer EDES 353-001/002 DISE W27",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit:   Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE)  Course code and title: EDES 353-001/002. Teaching Secondary Mathematics 1. Description : Provides insight and understanding of the Quebec secondary mathematics program. Focuses on key areas of what secondary mathematics teachers need to know and be able to do to support students' development of mathematical understanding (focus on mathematics content, students' reasoning, and pedagogy). This course is not Team Taught or offered online. Term: Winter 2027 Course Credits : 3 Location: Education Building (EDUC 436) Schedule: Wednesday, 05:35 pm-08:25 pm Appointment dates: December 21, 2026 - April 30, 2027 Teaching Qualification Requirements (TQRs): Education 1.MA in a relevant field (i.e. mathematics education) and/or extensive relevant experience as a school educator/teacher/pedagogue/community educator  2.PhD or equivalent in a relevant field is an asset  Experience 1. Expert knowledge of: Secondary mathematics pedagogy, as outlined in the course description  Mathematics content and practices related to secondary mathematics curricula  Research on secondary science pedagogy   Research on secondary students’ mathematical thinking and practice  2. Experience as a master teacher/instructor in mathematics, science, or a related field in the Quebec educational system 3. Knowledge of Quebec Education Program (QEP)  4. Familiarity with the 13 professional competencies specified by the Ministère de l’Éducation  Other 1.Previous successful experience teaching similar course(s) at the undergraduate or graduate level  2.Knowledge of the impact and proven record integrating pedagogical approaches anchored to equity, diversity and inclusion  3.Familiarity using myCourses, ZOOM and other similar online platforms to facilitate quality teaching and learning experiences   4.Familiarity teaching blended classes is an asset   5.Familiarity with the application of a variety of digital teaching and learning tools  6.Familiarity of and/or experience with practice-based pedagogies in mathematics teacher education is an asset. Other information: 1.Commitment to working with a team of committed and engaged instructors. 2.Must be available to attend course coordination and planning meeting minimum of 2 weeks in advance of course start date. Posting Period: October 1- October 15, 2026 Deadline to apply : October 15 (11:59 PM) Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course Title: Teaching Secondary Mathematics 1 Subject Code: EDES 353 001/002 Location: Education Building Schedule: Wednesday 05:35 pm-08:25 pm Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-15 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/Course-Lecturer-EDER-609-001-DISE-W27_JR0000081350": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer EDER 609-001 DISE W27",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course code and title: EDER 609-001. Education and Philosophical Thought. Description: An analysis of the educational implications of various philosophical positions concerning the nature of reality and the nature of knowledge. This course is not Team Taught or offered online. Term : Winter 2027 Course Credits:  3 Course Location: SH680 1822 Course Schedule: Monday, 05:35 pm-08:25 pm Appointment dates: December 21, 2026 - April 30, 2027 Teaching Qualification Requirements (TQRs): Education   1. PhD (in exceptional cases, PhD candidates and master teachers with an MA with extensive relevant experience will be considered) Experience   1.Expert knowledge and experience in course content including: knowledge of philosophers and philosophies of education from around the world and from non-dominant identities. 2.Knowledge of the Quebec Education program (QEP) 3.Familiarity with the 13 professional competencies specified in the Ministère de l’Éducation 4.Previous successful teaching similar course(s) at the university level 5.Experience teaching in the Quebec school system an asset Other 1.Ability to engage in non-traditional online pedagogies a plus. Posting period: October 1 - October 15, 2026 Application deadline: October 15 (11:59 PM) Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. 