    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Strathcona-Music/Course-Lecturer-Positions--1504----Department-of-Performance---Winter-2027_JR0000080187-1": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer Positions (15.04) - Department of Performance - Winter 2027",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). MCLIU Course Lecturer positions for the Winter 2027 semester in the Department of Performance Hiring Unit (\"Music Performance\"). Use this form to submit your application to any of the positions listed below. You will have the opportunity to list your ranked top choices of course(s) in your application. Positions currently available: MUPG 415-001: Brass Orchestral Excerpts MUPG 571-001: Free Improvisation 1 MUEN 572-001: Cappella Antica MUEN 592-001: Chamber Jazz Ensemble MUEN 595-001: Jazz Ensembles (Big Band 1) MUEN 595-002: Jazz Ensembles (Big Band 1) MUEN 595-003: Jazz Ensembles (Big Band 1) MUEN 595-004: Jazz Ensembles (Big Band 1) MUEN 595-003: Jazz Ensembles - (Guitar Jazz Ensemble 1) MUEN 595-004: Jazz Ensembles - (Guitar Jazz Ensemble 2) MUJZ 161-001: Jazz Materials 2 MUJZ 171-001: Jazz Keyboard Proficiency 2 MUJZ 171-002: Jazz Keyboard Proficiency 2 MUJZ 261-001: Jazz Arranging 2 MUJZ 261-002: Jazz Arranging 2 MUJZ 341-001: Jazz Composition 1 MUJZ 341-002: Jazz Composition 1 MUJZ 601-001: Grad. Jazz Pedagogy MUEN 569-001: Tabla Ensemble MUPG 416-001: Percussion Orchestral Excerpts. MUEN 581-001: Introduction to Ensemble Playing for Pianists MUPG 350-001: Introduction to Piano Pedagogy MUPG 412-001: Cello Orchestral Excerpts MUPG 213-001: German Diction MUPG 213-002: German Diction MUPG 590-001: Vocal Styles and Conventions MUPG 414-001: Woodwinds Orchestral Excerpts MUJZ 424-001: Jazz Improv/Musicianship 4 MUJZ 224-002: Jazz Improv/Musicianship 2 Posting Date: October 1, 2026 Application Deadline: October 16, 2026, 11:59 p.m. If needed, follow this guide for submitting an application depending on your status in Workday: If you have an active position in Workday (not terminated), use How to Apply for a Job (for Internal Candidates): https://general-knowledgebase.mcgill.ca/spaces/SHRKB/pages/54632206/How+to+Apply+for+a+Job+for+Internal+Candidates If you do not have an active position in Workday (including prior or terminated employees), use How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates): https://www.mcgill.ca/hr/files/hr/workday_guide_for_candidates_extenal_en.pdf McGill University is committed to equity and diversity within its community and values academic rigour and excellence. We welcome and encourage applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to engage productively with diverse communities. At McGill, research that reflects diverse intellectual traditions, methodologies, and modes of dissemination and translation is valued and encouraged. Candidates are invited to demonstrate their research impact both within and across academic disciplines and in other sectors, such as government, communities, or industry. McGill further recognizes and fairly considers the impact of leaves (e.g., family care or health-related) that may contribute to career interruptions or slowdowns. Candidates are encouraged to signal any leave that affected productivity, or that may have had an effect on their career path. This information will be considered to ensure the equitable assessment of the candidate’s record. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated equity groups to self-identify. It further seeks to ensure the equitable treatment and full inclusion of persons with disabilities by striving for the implementation of universal design principles transversally, across all facets of the University community, and through  accommodation policies and procedures . Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/Course-Lecturer-EDER-607-001-DISE-W27_JR0000081323": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer EDER 607-001 DISE W27",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course code and title: EDER 607-001. Ethics and Values in Education. Description : Considers education as a concept and practice influenced by values (ethical, religious, aesthetic, cultural, political, etc.). Includes a critical examination of selected approaches to values education. This course is not Team Taught or offered online. Course term: Winter 2027 Course Credits:  3 Course Schedule : Mondays, 05:35 pm-08:25 pm Location : SH680 451 Appointment dates: December 21, 2026 - April 30, 2026 Teaching Qualification Requirements (TQRs): Education: 1.Master educator with an MA in a relevant field (e.g. philosophy of education, moral and/or political philosophy, educational ethics) 2.Experience as an educator in the pre-K to graduation or higher education sectors is an asset 3.PhD or equivalent in a relevant field is an asset Experience: Expert knowledge of: Main philosophical theories of ethics, political philosophy and value theory – including but not limited to those from Western analytic and continental philosophical traditions, such as: moral philosophy, social and political philosophy, aesthetics, feminist philosophy, critical philosophy of race and the philosophy of religion Traditions and approaches that apply philosophical theories of ethics to questions and problems of educational theory, practice and policy, including consequentialist and non-consequentialist theories of ethics The field of educational ethics and associated methodologies such as normative case studies Familiarity with contemporary theoretical approaches that employ interdisciplinary perspectives on moral education (e.g. philosophy and developmental psychology; non-ideal ethical theory). Other: 1.Previous successful experience teaching similar course(s) at the graduate level. 2.Knowledge of the impact and proven record integrating pedagogical approaches anchored to equity, diversity and inclusion 3.Familiarity using myCourses, ZOOM and other similar online platforms to facilitate quality teaching and learning experiences 4.Familiarity teaching blended classes is an asset 5.Familiarity with the application of a variety of digital teaching and learning tools Other information: 1.Commitment to working with a team of committed and engaged instructors. 2.Must be available to attend course coordination and planning meeting minimum of 2 weeks in advance of course start date   Posting Period: October 1- October 15, 2026 Deadline to apply: October 15 (11:59 PM) Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writin g. Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course Title: Ethics and Values in Education Subject Code: EDER 607 001 Location: SH680 451 Schedule: Monday 05:35 pm-08:25 pm Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-15 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Arts-Building/ENGL----Course-Lecturer---Winter-2027_JR0000081529-1": {
      "title": "ENGL -  Course Lecturer - Winter 2027",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). McGill University Department of English  Winter 2027 - Course Lecturer - Job Posting 7 Key academic dates | Important Dates for Students - McGill University The Department of English invites applications for a Course Lecturer positions to teach during the Winter 2027 term. Please note that Course Lecturers have signed a new Collective Agreement available at: 2024-12-04_mcliu_collective_agreement_final.pdf Please note that external candidates or former employees must apply as an external candidate (with their personal email address).   IMPORTANT NOTES: Candidates who are active in Workday, meaning they currently have a position (and salary) that has already started, must apply as an INTERNAL candidate using their McGill email address. Candidates who do not have a current or upcoming position in Workday must apply as an EXTERNAL candidate using their personal email address . Course Lecturers must be available for the official course schedule throughout the entire term, including the make-up class day on April 13/14, 2027, for the Winter 2027 term. Please consult the important dates calendar by clicking this link: Important Dates 2026–2027 If you are applying for multiple courses, please indicate your preferences in descending order.   Posting period and application deadline:   October 1st to 15th, 2026 Required documents :   All candidates : Cover letter; Proposed course outline or full syllabus;   For candidates who have previously taught in the Department: Updated Curriculum vitae; International applicants: submission of Work Permit is not required, unless the Work Permit has expired.   For new candidates: Curriculum Vitae; International applicants: copy of your Work Permit .   Available Positions :   ENGL 204 - English Literature and the Bible (3 credits - CRN 2506) Salary: $11,824 Teaching Qualification Requirements (TQRs): Demonstrated research and teaching excellence in the field of English literature and the Bible. Schedule: January 5th to April 14th, 2027 Tuesday & Thursday from 4:05 p.m.–5:25 p.m. Course description: This course will examine the literary dimensions of the Bible including structure, style, and meaning as well as its status as Sacred Book. The influence of the Bible-as-metatext on the secular literature of the West will be the focus of the discussion. ENGL 372 - Stage Scenery and Lighting 2 (3 credits - CRN 7437) Salary: $11,824   Teaching Qualification Requirements (TQRs): Graduate from a program specializing in theatre production; working experience in technical production, design, and management of theatre and/or live events; experience teaching in University settings and on university theatrical productions. Schedule: January 5th to April 14th, 2027 Tuesday & Thursday from 10:05 a.m.–11:25 a.m. Course description: Aspects of stage scenery and theatrical lighting.  ENGL 500 - Middle English (CRN 2539 – 3 credits) Salary: $11,824 Teaching Qualification Requirements (TQRs): Demonstrated research and teaching excellence in the literature of the Middle English period. Schedule: January 5th to April 14th, 2027 Tuesday & Thursday from 11:35 a.m.–02:25 p.m. Course description : A study of works in Middle English. ENGL 516 - Shakespeare (CRN 2541 – 3 credits) Salary: $11,824 Teaching Qualification Requirements (TQRs): Demonstrated research and teaching excellence in the field of Shakespeare studies.  Schedule: January 5th to April 14th, 2027 Tuesday & Thursday from 4:05 p.m.–5:25 p.m. Course description: A seminar on the works of Shakespeare. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- Université McGill Département d’anglais Hiver 2027 - Postes de Chargé de cours – Affichage 7 https://www.mcgill.ca/importantdates/key-dates      Le Département d’anglais offre un poste de Chargé de cours pour la session d’hiver 2027.   Veuillez noter que les Chargés de cours ont signé une nouvelle Convention collective disponible en ligne à l’adresse suivante : 2024-12-04_mcliu_collective_agreement_final.pdf   Les candidats sont priés de remplir le formulaire de candidature en ligne de Workday et de téléverser les documents requis.   NOTES IMPORTANTES: 1) Les candidats 'actifs', qui sont déjà dans workday avec un emploi (et salaire) qui a déjà débuté, doivent postuler en tant que candidat INTERNE avec leur adresse courriel McGill . 2)  Les candidats qui n’ont aucun poste en cours ni à venir dans workday, devront postuler en tant que candidat EXTERNE avec leur adresse courriel personnelle . 3)   Les chargés de cours doivent être disponibles pour l’horaire officiel du cours pendant tout le trimestre, y compris la journée de reprise de cours le 13/14 avril 2027 pour la session d’hiver 2027. Veuillez consulter le calendrier des dates importantes en cliquant sur ce lien :  Dates importantes 2026-2027 . 4)  Si vous postulez pour plusieurs cours, veuillez indiquer vos préférences par ordre décroissant. Période d’affichage et date limite pour soumettre un dossier de candidature : Du 1er au 15 octobre 2026 Documents requis :   Tous les candidats : Lettre de motivation; Plan de cours proposé ou programme complet; Candidats ayant déjà enseigné au Département d’anglais :  Curriculum vitae à jour; Candidats internationaux : copie du Permis de travail , dans le cas où le permis serait expiré. Nouveaux candidats : Curriculum vitae Candidats internationaux : copie du Permis de travail . Postes disponibles:   ENGL 204 - English Literature and the Bible (3 crédits - CRN 2506) Salaire : $11,824 Exigences de qualifications pour l’enseignement (EQE) : Excellence démontrée en recherche et en enseignement dans le domaine de la littérature anglaise et de la Bible. Horaire : 5 janvier au 14 avril 2027 Mardi et jeudi de 16 h 05 à 17 h 25 Description du cours:  Ce cours examinera les dimensions littéraires de la Bible, notamment sa structure, son style et sa signification, ainsi que son statut de Livre sacré. L’influence de la Bible en tant que métatexte sur la littérature profane de l’Occident constituera le principal objet de la discussion. ENGL 372 - Stage Scenery and Lighting 2 (3 crédits - CRN 7437) Salaire : $11,824 Exigences de qualifications pour l’enseignement (EQE) : Diplômé d’un programme spécialisé en production théâtrale; expérience professionnelle dans la production technique, la conception et la gestion de théâtre et/ou d’événements en direct; expérience d’enseignement dans des établissements universitaires et dans des productions théâtrales universitaires. Horaire : 5 janvier au 14 avril 2027 Mardi et jeudi 10 h 05- 11 h 25  Description du cours:  Aspects du décor de scène et de l’éclairage théâtral. ENGL 500 - Middle English (3 crédits - CRN 2539) Salaire : 11 824 $ Exigences de qualification pour l’enseignement (EQE) : Excellence démontrée en recherche et en enseignement dans le domaine de la littérature de la période du moyen anglais. Horaire : Du 5 janvier au 14 avril 2027 Vendredi, de 11 h 35 à 14 h 25 Description du cours : Étude d’œuvres en moyen anglais. ENGL 516 Shakespeare (CRN 2541 – 3 crédits) Salaire : 11 824 $ Exigences de qualification pour l’enseignement (EQE) : Excellence démontrée en recherche et en enseignement dans le domaine des études shakespeariennes. Horaire : Du 5 janvier au 14 avril 2027 Mardi et jeudi, de 16 h 05 à 17 h 25 Description du cours:  Un séminaire sur les œuvres de Shakespeare. L’Université McGill est une institution de langue anglaise dans laquelle la majorité des activités d’enseignement et de recherche s’effectuent en anglais, rendant essentielle l’utilisation de l’anglais pour la communication orale et écrite. McGill University is committed to equity and diversity within its community and values academic rigour and excellence. We welcome and encourage applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to engage productively with diverse communities. At McGill, research that reflects diverse intellectual traditions, methodologies, and modes of dissemination and translation is valued and encouraged. Candidates are invited to demonstrate their research impact both within and across academic disciplines and in other sectors, such as government, communities, or industry. McGill further recognizes and fairly considers the impact of leaves (e.g., family care or health-related) that may contribute to career interruptions or slowdowns. Candidates are encouraged to signal any leave that affected productivity, or that may have had an effect on their career path. This information will be considered to ensure the equitable assessment of the candidate’s record. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated equity groups to self-identify. It further seeks to ensure the equitable treatment and full inclusion of persons with disabilities by striving for the implementation of universal design principles transversally, across all facets of the University community, and through  accommodation policies and procedures . Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Strathcona-Music/Course-Lecturer-Positions--1504----Department-of-Music-Research---Winter-2027_JR0000080185-1": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer Positions (15.04) - Department of Music Research - Winter 2027",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). MCLIU Course Lecturer positions for the Winter 2027 semester in the Department of Music Research Hiring Unit. Use this form to submit your application to any of the positions listed below. You will have the opportunity to list your ranked top choices of course(s) in your application. Positions currently available: MUGT 215-001: Basic Conducting Techniques MUGT 303-001: Global Percussion. MUIT 250-001: Guitar Techniques MUPD 200-001: Intro to Music Marketing MUPD 235-001: Music as a Profession 2 MUSP 124-001: Jazz Ear Training 2 MUSP 141-###: Musicianship Training 2 MUSP 171-###: Musicianship (Keyboard) 2 MUSP 241-###: Musicianship Training 4 MUSP 363-001: Topics in Global Musicianship MUHL 211-001: The Art of Listening MUHL 286-001: Critical Thinking About Music MUPD 204-001: Production for Digital Media 1 Posting Date: October 1, 2026 Application Deadline: October 16, 2026, 11:59 p.m. If needed, follow this guide for submitting an application depending on your status in Workday: If you have an active position in Workday (not terminated), use How to Apply for a Job (for Internal Candidates): https://general-knowledgebase.mcgill.ca/spaces/SHRKB/pages/54632206/How+to+Apply+for+a+Job+for+Internal+Candidates If you do not have an active position in Workday (including prior or terminated employees), use How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates): https://www.mcgill.ca/hr/files/hr/workday_guide_for_candidates_extenal_en.pdf McGill University is committed to equity and diversity within its community and values academic rigour and excellence. We welcome and encourage applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to engage productively with diverse communities. At McGill, research that reflects diverse intellectual traditions, methodologies, and modes of dissemination and translation is valued and encouraged. Candidates are invited to demonstrate their research impact both within and across academic disciplines and in other sectors, such as government, communities, or industry. McGill further recognizes and fairly considers the impact of leaves (e.g., family care or health-related) that may contribute to career interruptions or slowdowns. Candidates are encouraged to signal any leave that affected productivity, or that may have had an effect on their career path. This information will be considered to ensure the equitable assessment of the candidate’s record. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated equity groups to self-identify. It further seeks to ensure the equitable treatment and full inclusion of persons with disabilities by striving for the implementation of universal design principles transversally, across all facets of the University community, and through  accommodation policies and procedures . Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority."
