    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/Course-Lecturer-EDES-361-001-DISE-W27_JR0000081396": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer EDES 361-001 DISE W27",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course Description: EDES 361-001. Teaching Secondary English 1. Description : Examination of appropriate materials related to the high school English programs; exploration of various techniques of teaching language, literature, writing and dramatics in the secondary school. This course is not Team Taught or offered online. Term: Winter 2027 Course Credits : 3 Location: Education Building (EDUC 113) Schedule:   Monday & Wednesday, 11:35 am-12:55 pm Appointment dates: December 21, 2026 - April 30, 2027 Teaching Qualification Requirements (TQRs): Education: 1.MA in a relevant field (i.e. English Language Arts-Secondary programs). 2.PhD or equivalent in a relevant field is an asset. Experience: 1.Expert knowledge of: Quebec Education Plan (QEP) Secondary English Language Arts (SELA) competencies & Progression of Learning. Instructional strategies for ELA. Methods of evaluation in different ELA contexts . Lesson designs and learning evaluation situations using Understanding by Design framework. 2.Experience as a Secondary master/teacher/instructor in the Quebec educational system. 3.Familiarity with the 13 professional competencies specified by the Ministère de l’Éducation . Other: 1.Previous successful experience teaching similar course(s) at the undergraduate or graduate level. 2.Knowledge of the impact and proven record integrating pedagogical approaches anchored to equity, diversity and inclusion. 3.Familiarity using myCourses, ZOOM and other similar online platforms to facilitate quality teaching and learning experiences. 4.Familiarity teaching blended classes is an asset. 5.Familiarity with the application of a variety of digital teaching and learning tools. Other information: 1.Commitment to working with a team of committed and engaged instructors  2.Must be available to attend course coordination and planning meeting in advance of course start date 3.A commitment to working collaboratively in planning and delivering the course Posting Period: October 1-15, 2026 Deadline to apply : October 15 (11:59 PM) Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hiring Unit: Department of Integrated Studies in Education (DISE) Course Title: Teaching Secondary English 1. Subject Code: EDES 361 001 Location: Education Building Schedule: Monday & Wednesday 11:35 am-12:55 pm Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-15 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
